window.NOTES=[{"id": "intro", "n": 0, "title": "How to use these notes", "marks": 0, "html": "<p>Target 90 of 100: the exam is 100 one-mark questions in 2 hours, pass mark 50, no negative marking, so never leave a question blank. These notes follow the March 2026 revised workbook, which reflects the SEBI (Mutual Funds) Regulations, 2026 and the new expense limits from 1 April 2026.</p>\n<p><strong>What the real paper feels like.</strong> A candidate who sat the exam in October 2026 found it harder than recall drills suggest. About <strong>20 to 30 questions</strong> gave two or three statements and asked which is true or which is false. <strong>Fewer than 10</strong> needed any calculation. Several questions were \"tweaks\" that test whether you understand a concept, such as asking what the <strong>numerator</strong> of a ratio represents rather than its value. Learn each rule well enough to spot a near-miss: a swapped number, a swapped body (trustees vs AMC), or an added \"only\". Each chapter now ends with <strong>Exam traps</strong>, and Practice has a <strong>Statement drill</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Unit</th>\n<th>Chapter</th>\n<th>Exam weight</th>\n<th>Practice Qs</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Investment Landscape</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>56</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Concept and Role of a Mutual Fund</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>52</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Legal Structure of Mutual Funds</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>43</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Legal and Regulatory Framework</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>75</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Scheme Related Information</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>68</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Fund Distribution and Channel Management</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>41</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>NAV, TER and Pricing of Units</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>58</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>Taxation</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>Investor Services</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>101</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>Risk, Return and Performance of Funds</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>53</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>11</td>\n<td>Mutual Fund Scheme Performance</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>53</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>Mutual Fund Scheme Selection</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>100</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Chapters 9 and 12 carry 30 marks between them, and 4 and 5 another 20. Half the paper sits in four chapters.</p>\n<p><strong>Suggested two-week plan (one session a day):</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Day</th>\n<th>Session</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Chapter 1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Chapters 2 and 3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Chapter 4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Chapter 5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Chapter 6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Chapters 7 and 8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>Chapter 9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>Chapter 10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>Chapter 11</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>Chapter 12</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>11</td>\n<td>Mocks 1 and 2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>Mocks 3 and 4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>13</td>\n<td>Mock 5 and weak-area revision</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Big changes in the March 2026 workbook.</strong> Know these cold:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>SEBI (Mutual Funds) Regulations, 2026</strong> replace the 1996 Regulations. Schedule numbers moved: valuation = <strong>Seventh</strong>, ad code = <strong>Fifth</strong>, code of conduct = <strong>Fourth</strong>, investment restrictions = <strong>Sixth</strong>.</li>\n<li>New expense limits (<strong>base expense ratio</strong>): equity <strong>2.10%</strong> and non-equity <strong>1.85%</strong> on the first Rs 500 cr; index/ETF <strong>0.90%</strong>; brokerage <strong>0.06% / 0.02%</strong>; the extra <strong>0.05% is gone</strong>.</li>\n<li>Categories: equity <strong>13</strong>, debt <strong>17</strong>, hybrid <strong>7</strong>; <strong>Life Cycle Funds</strong> replace solution-oriented (retirement/children's) funds.</li>\n<li>Distributors earn <strong>trail commission only</strong>. Upfront commission and transaction charges were withdrawn by SEBI in August 2025.</li>\n<li>Investors may name <strong>up to 10 nominees</strong>.</li>\n</ul>"}, {"id": "ch1", "n": 1, "title": "Investment Landscape", "marks": 8, "html": "<h4>Basics</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Point</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Financial goal</td>\n<td>Objective + amount + timeline = <strong>financial goal</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hospitalisation, theft, fire</td>\n<td>Cover with <strong>emergency fund + insurance</strong>, not investments</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pool approach</td>\n<td>Flaw: <strong>horizon unknown</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Saving vs investing</td>\n<td><strong>Saving precedes investing</strong>; \"saving\" comes from \"safe\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mutual fund</td>\n<td>A <strong>different way of investing</strong>, not a different product</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Compounding examples</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Example</th>\n<th>Horizon</th>\n<th>Value</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Shalini: Rs 50 lakh at 8%</td>\n<td>10 years</td>\n<td><strong>Rs 1,07,94,625</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 30,000 at 6%</td>\n<td>1 yr</td>\n<td><strong>31,800</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 30,000 at 6%</td>\n<td>10 yrs</td>\n<td><strong>53,725</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 30,000 at 6%</td>\n<td>20 yrs</td>\n<td><strong>96,214</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 10,000 at 8%</td>\n<td>5 yrs</td>\n<td><strong>14,693</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 10,000 at 8%</td>\n<td>10 yrs</td>\n<td><strong>21,589</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 10,000 at 8%</td>\n<td>20 yrs</td>\n<td><strong>46,610</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 10,000 at 8%</td>\n<td>30 yrs</td>\n<td><strong>1,00,627</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>At 8%: 100 units buys <strong>68</strong> after 5 yrs, <strong>46</strong> after 10.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Evaluating an investment</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Point</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Top 3 evaluation factors</td>\n<td><strong>safety, liquidity, returns</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Exit penalty</td>\n<td>Hits <strong>returns</strong>, not liquidity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Nominal</strong></td>\n<td>Before inflation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>real</strong></td>\n<td>After inflation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Listed equity</td>\n<td>Liquid but <strong>unfit for short-term needs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Four asset classes: <strong>Real estate, Commodities, Equity, Fixed income</strong>.</li>\n<li>Only financial form: <strong>equity and bonds</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Asset class features</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Asset class</th>\n<th>Key points</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Real estate</td>\n<td><strong>location</strong> is key; illiquid; <strong>not divisible</strong>; self-occupied home = <strong>expense</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Commodities</td>\n<td>Only <strong>commodities</strong> give no intermittent cash flow; physical gold = no regular income</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Commodity derivatives</td>\n<td>Aren't investments: <strong>leveraged + short-term</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonds</td>\n<td>Bought at issue, held to maturity: <strong>no capital gain</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sensex</td>\n<td>Base <strong>100 in 1979</strong>, <strong>82,269 by 30 Jan 2026</strong>, <strong>\\~15.4% p.a.</strong> (before dividends)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Table 1.1: where products fit</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Product</th>\n<th>Asset class</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>PPF, SSY, SCSS, POMIS, endowment/money-back</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Fixed Income</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>REITs, InvITs, REMF</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Real Estate</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>coins, art, stamps</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Others</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Types of risk and how they are measured</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Risk</th>\n<th>Key point</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Credit risk</td>\n<td>Causes: borrower's <strong>ability or intention</strong>; measured by <strong>rating + spreads</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Own government's bonds</td>\n<td><strong>safest, lowest rate</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pager industry</td>\n<td><strong>industry-specific</strong> risk</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Market-wide vs company-specific</td>\n<td><strong>Market-wide risk cannot be diversified</strong>; company-specific can</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rates vs bond prices</td>\n<td>Rates up, bond price <strong>down</strong>; <strong>longer maturity = bigger swing</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Volatility</td>\n<td>Measured by <strong>variance, SD, beta, modified duration</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Risk strategies</td>\n<td><strong>avoid, take a position, diversify</strong>; lay investor = <strong>diversify</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Behavioural biases</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Behaviour</th>\n<th>Name</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Dominant emotions</td>\n<td><strong>fear, greed, hope</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 5,000 loss hurts more than gain</td>\n<td><strong>loss aversion</strong> (Kahneman &amp; Tversky)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Decide first, seek proof later</td>\n<td><strong>confirmation bias</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\"Known devil vs unknown angel\"</td>\n<td><strong>familiarity bias</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bull run drives over-allocation</td>\n<td><strong>recency bias</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>IT employee with only tech stocks</td>\n<td><strong>interest of the investor</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Remedy for biases</td>\n<td>Third opinion from an <strong>RIA or MFD</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Risk profile</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Element</th>\n<th>Made of</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Risk profile</td>\n<td><strong>need + ability + willingness</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ability</td>\n<td><strong>finances + horizon</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Willingness</td>\n<td><strong>psychology</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Allocation and rebalancing</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Approach</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Strategic</td>\n<td><strong>fixed target mix</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tactical/dynamic</td>\n<td><strong>improve risk-adjusted return</strong>; for <strong>seasoned investors with large surplus</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rebalancing</td>\n<td><strong>sell what rose, buy what fell</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rebalancing example</td>\n<td>50:50 with A +20%, B −5% on Rs 1,000 each: <strong>sell Rs 125 of A</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Passive breach rebalancing</td>\n<td><strong>30 business days</strong>; excludes index funds/ETFs; <strong>not applicable to overnight funds</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>DIY hidden costs: <strong>time + mistakes</strong>; 2% fee on Rs 10 lakh = <strong>\\~Rs 20,000/yr</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li>An exit penalty hurts <strong>returns</strong>, not liquidity.</li>\n<li><strong>Market-wide</strong> risk cannot be diversified; only company-specific risk can.</li>\n<li>Ability to take risk = <strong>finances + horizon</strong>; willingness = <strong>psychology</strong>, not finances.</li>\n<li>Deciding first and seeking proof later = <strong>confirmation</strong> bias; 'known devil vs unknown angel' = <strong>familiarity</strong> bias; over-allocating after a bull run = <strong>recency</strong> bias.</li>\n<li>A self-occupied home is an <strong>expense</strong>, not an investment.</li>\n<li>REITs, InvITs and REMF = <strong>Real Estate</strong>, not equity; PPF, SSY, SCSS, POMIS and endowment policies = <strong>Fixed Income</strong>; coins, art, stamps = <strong>Others</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Commodities</strong> are the only asset class with no intermittent cash flow, not fixed income.</li>\n<li>Credit risk is measured by <strong>rating and spreads</strong>; variance, SD, beta and modified duration measure <strong>volatility</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n"}, {"id": "ch2", "n": 2, "title": "Concept and Role of a Mutual Fund", "marks": 6, "html": "<ul>\n<li>You invest <strong>through</strong> a mutual fund, not <strong>in</strong> one; it is a <strong>different way of investing</strong>, not a different product.</li>\n<li>A mutual fund is set up as a <strong>trust</strong>. Profits and losses belong <strong>only to unitholders</strong>; everyone else earns a <strong>fee or commission</strong>.</li>\n<li>Each separate pool of money = a <strong>scheme</strong>, with a pre-announced <strong>investment objective</strong>. Investment policy = <strong>asset allocation + investment style</strong>, disclosed in the <strong>SID</strong>.</li>\n<li>MFs act as a <strong>market stabiliser</strong>: in <strong>2022 and 2025</strong> MF inflows countered heavy <strong>FPI</strong> selling.</li>\n<li>MF is a <strong>pass-through vehicle</strong>; the fund manager controls only <strong>his own skill</strong>, not the market or securities.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Key terms</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Term</th>\n<th>What it means</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Face value</td>\n<td>Typically <strong>Rs 10</strong> (can differ, e.g. <strong>Rs 100</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unit capital</td>\n<td><strong>Units × face value</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AUM</td>\n<td><strong>NAV × units outstanding</strong>; AMCs are ranked by <strong>AUM</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NAV</td>\n<td><strong>Net realisable value per unit</strong> if the scheme were liquidated</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mark to market</td>\n<td>Valuing each security at market price, <strong>daily</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>IDCW</td>\n<td>Old \"dividend\" option, now <strong>Income Distribution cum Capital Withdrawal</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Recurring expenses</td>\n<td>Charged as a <strong>% of AUM</strong>; they <strong>lower the NAV</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Advantages and limitations</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Advantages</th>\n<th>Limitations</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Diversification from as little as <strong>Rs 500</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No customisation</strong> (PMS gives it)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Transparency: <strong>SID, SAI, KIM + portfolio + NAV</strong>, open to <strong>prospective investors</strong> too</td>\n<td><strong>Choice overload</strong> (SEBI <strong>categorisation</strong> was the answer)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Tax deferral</strong>: MFs don't pay tax on income; growth option defers tax</td>\n<td><strong>No control over costs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>ELSS</strong>: up to <strong>Rs 1,50,000</strong> under <strong>Sec 80C</strong>, <strong>Old Tax Regime</strong> only</td>\n<td><strong>No guaranteed returns</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SIP</strong> (invest), <strong>SWP</strong> (withdraw), <strong>STP</strong> (transfer)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Open-ended, close-ended, interval and ETF</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Structure</th>\n<th>Buying and selling</th>\n<th>Key points</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Open-ended</td>\n<td>Buy or sell <strong>any time after the NFO</strong></td>\n<td>Unit capital <strong>keeps changing</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Close-ended</td>\n<td>Buy <strong>only in the NFO</strong>; exit through the exchange</td>\n<td><strong>Fixed maturity</strong>; <strong>compulsorily listed</strong> (<strong>except ELSS</strong>); unit capital <strong>fixed</strong>; usually trades at a <strong>discount to NAV</strong> (the buyer has the bargaining power)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Interval</td>\n<td>Close-ended, but <strong>opens at intervals</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Listed</strong>; transaction period <strong>min 2 days</strong>; interval period <strong>15 days</strong> (workbook wording)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ETF</td>\n<td>Trades <strong>all day</strong> at multiple prices; needs a <strong>demat account</strong></td>\n<td>Tracks NAV closely; <strong>Silver ETF</strong> now allowed</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Active vs passive</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Active</th>\n<th>Passive (index / ETF)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Aim</td>\n<td>Beat the market</td>\n<td>Track the index</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cost</td>\n<td>Higher</td>\n<td><strong>Low</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fund manager's choice</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>MF Lite</strong> = <strong>Chapter X</strong> of the MF Regulations 2026: a lighter framework for <strong>passive</strong> schemes only (index funds, ETFs, FoFs).</p>\n<h4>SEBI categorisation (2026 circular)</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Number of schemes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity</td>\n<td><strong>13</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt</td>\n<td><strong>17</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hybrid</td>\n<td><strong>7</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Life Cycle Funds</td>\n<td>New category</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other</td>\n<td><strong>2</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Market cap: <strong>Large 1–100</strong>, <strong>Mid 101–250</strong>, <strong>Small 251+</strong>, by <strong>full market cap</strong>.</li>\n<li>One scheme per category, <strong>except</strong>: index funds/ETFs on different indices, FoFs with different underlyings, sector/thematic funds on different sectors.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Equity schemes: mandate</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Minimum in equity / rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi cap</td>\n<td><strong>≥75%</strong> equity, with <strong>≥25% each</strong> in large, mid and small</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Large cap</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong> in large caps</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Large &amp; Mid cap</td>\n<td><strong>35% + 35%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mid cap</td>\n<td><strong>65%</strong> in mid caps</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Small cap</td>\n<td><strong>65%</strong> in small caps</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dividend yield</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Value</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong>; separate from contra</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Contra</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong>; an AMC can offer both value and contra if portfolio overlap is <strong>≤50%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Focused</td>\n<td><strong>Max 30 stocks</strong>, <strong>80%</strong> equity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sectoral</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong>; separate from thematic</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Thematic</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong>; overlap with other sectoral/thematic and equity schemes <strong>≤50%</strong> (<strong>except large cap</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ELSS – Tax Saver Fund</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong> + <strong>3-year lock-in</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Flexi cap</td>\n<td><strong>65%</strong>, any mix of market caps</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Equity schemes may put the <strong>residual</strong> in money market, <strong>gold and silver</strong> instruments and <strong>InvITs</strong>.</p>\n<h4>Debt schemes: mandate</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Rule (duration = Macaulay)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Overnight</td>\n<td><strong>1 day</strong>; may put <strong>≤5%</strong> in G-secs/T-bills (<strong>≤30 days</strong>) for margin</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Liquid</td>\n<td>Up to <strong>91 days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ultra-Short-Term</td>\n<td><strong>3–6 months</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ultra Short to Short Term (was low duration)</td>\n<td><strong>6–12 months</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Money market</td>\n<td>Up to <strong>1 year</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Short Term</td>\n<td><strong>1–3 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Medium Term</td>\n<td><strong>3–4 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Medium to Long Term</td>\n<td><strong>4–7 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Long Term</td>\n<td><strong>&gt; 7 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dynamic Term</td>\n<td><strong>Any</strong> duration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Corporate bond</td>\n<td><strong>80% in AA+ and above</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Credit risk</td>\n<td><strong>65% in AA and below</strong> (AA+ excluded); name can't stress return (<strong>no \"high yield\", \"credit opportunities\"</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Banking and PSU Debt</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gilt</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong> in G-secs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10-year constant maturity Gilt</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong> in G-secs, duration <strong>= 10 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Floating Interest Rates Fund</td>\n<td><strong>65%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sectoral (debt) Fund</td>\n<td><strong>80%</strong> in one sector, <strong>only AA+ and above</strong>; Financial Services, Energy, Infrastructure, Housing, Real Estate</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Hybrid schemes: mandate</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Mandate</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Conservative hybrid</td>\n<td>Debt <strong>75–90%</strong>, equity <strong>10–25%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Balanced hybrid</td>\n<td>Equity <strong>40–60%</strong>, <strong>no arbitrage</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Aggressive hybrid</td>\n<td>Equity <strong>65–80%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Balanced Advantage</td>\n<td><strong>Dynamic</strong> equity/debt</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi asset allocation</td>\n<td><strong>≥3 asset classes</strong>, <strong>≥10% each</strong>; <strong>foreign securities are not a separate class</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Arbitrage</td>\n<td><strong>65%</strong> equity; debt only in <strong>G-secs under 1 year</strong> and <strong>G-sec repo</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity savings</td>\n<td><strong>65%</strong> equity + <strong>10%</strong> debt; <strong>net equity 15–40%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>The category is now \"Balanced Hybrid <strong>and</strong> Aggressive Hybrid\".</li>\n<li>Hybrid schemes may put the <strong>residual</strong> in <strong>InvITs</strong> (not arbitrage funds), <strong>ETCDs, gold and silver ETFs</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>How hybrid funds are taxed (from Chapter 8)</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Hybrid</th>\n<th>Usual tax treatment</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Conservative hybrid</td>\n<td>Debt-oriented: <strong>slab rate</strong>, whatever the holding period</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Balanced hybrid</td>\n<td>35–65% equity: <strong>slab</strong> up to 24 months, <strong>12.5%</strong> after 24 months</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Aggressive hybrid</td>\n<td>Equity-oriented: <strong>20%</strong> up to 12 months, <strong>12.5%</strong> after; <strong>Rs 1.25 lakh</strong> exempt a year</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Arbitrage</td>\n<td>Equity-oriented: <strong>20% / 12.5%</strong> after 12 months</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity savings</td>\n<td>Equity-oriented: <strong>20% / 12.5%</strong> after 12 months</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Balanced Advantage, Multi asset</td>\n<td><strong>Depends on the actual equity share</strong>: above 65% = equity rules</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Tax follows the scheme's equity share: <strong>more than 65% listed Indian equity</strong> = equity-oriented; <strong>35–65%</strong> = slab, then 12.5% after 24 months; <strong>more than 65% debt</strong> = slab rate.</p>\n<h4>Life Cycle Funds</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Glide path</strong> across equity, debt, InvITs, ETCDs, gold and silver ETFs: equity falls, debt rises as maturity nears.</li>\n<li>Tenure <strong>5–30 years</strong> in <strong>multiples of 5</strong>; max <strong>6</strong> open for subscription per MF at a time.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Years to maturity (15-year fund)</th>\n<th>Equity</th>\n<th>Debt</th>\n<th>Gold, silver, ETCD, InvIT</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>10–15</td>\n<td><strong>65–80%</strong></td>\n<td>5–25%</td>\n<td>0–10%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5–10</td>\n<td><strong>50–65%</strong></td>\n<td>5–25%</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3–5</td>\n<td><strong>35–50%</strong></td>\n<td>25–50%</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1–3</td>\n<td><strong>20–35%</strong></td>\n<td>25–65%</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Under 1</td>\n<td><strong>5–20%</strong></td>\n<td>25–65%</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Other schemes (2) and other fund types</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Key feature</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Index fund / ETF</td>\n<td><strong>95%</strong> in index securities</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fund of funds (FoF)</td>\n<td><strong>95%</strong> in the underlying fund</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>FMP</td>\n<td>Close-ended debt; portfolio matches maturity; returns clearer but <strong>not guaranteed</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Target Maturity Fund</td>\n<td>Matures on a set date (<strong>2–14 years</strong>), <strong>listed</strong>, reduces <strong>reinvestment risk</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Capital protection fund</td>\n<td>Close-ended hybrid; e.g. <strong>Rs 90 in debt grows to Rs 100</strong>, rest in <strong>equity derivatives</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>IDF</td>\n<td>Close-ended, <strong>≥90%</strong> in infra debt; IDF-MF sponsored by <strong>banks and NBFCs</strong>; IDF-NBFC by <strong>banks and IFCs</strong> only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>REMF</td>\n<td>Real estate in cities named in the SEBI circular of <strong>2 May 2008</strong>; <strong>close-ended, listed</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>REITs / InvITs</td>\n<td><strong>Not MF schemes</strong>; REIT assets <strong>≥Rs 500 cr</strong>, offer <strong>≥Rs 250 cr</strong>; InvIT offer <strong>≥Rs 250 cr</strong>, assets <strong>≥Rs 500 cr</strong>; minimum lot <strong>Rs 10,000–15,000</strong>, traded lot <strong>1 unit</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ESG</td>\n<td>Under <strong>thematic</strong> equity; 6 strategies: exclusion, integration, best-in-class, impact, sustainable objectives, transition</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Smart beta</td>\n<td>Index-based but <strong>not market-cap weighted</strong> (e.g. equal weight)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Quant fund</td>\n<td>Model-driven; <strong>removes the human element</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Specialised Investment Fund (SIF)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fills the gap <strong>between MF and PMS</strong>; minimum <strong>Rs 10 lakh</strong> across strategies <strong>of the same AMC</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Every SIF strategy: max 25% unhedged short exposure</strong>; only <strong>one strategy per category</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Strategy</th>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n<th>Redemptions</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity Long-Short</td>\n<td>Equity</td>\n<td><strong>≥80%</strong> equity</td>\n<td><strong>Daily or less often</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity Ex-Top 100</td>\n<td>Equity</td>\n<td><strong>≥65%</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Daily or less often</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sector Rotation</td>\n<td>Equity</td>\n<td><strong>≥80%</strong>, <strong>max 4 sectors</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Daily or less often</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sectoral debt</td>\n<td>Debt (interval)</td>\n<td><strong>≥2 sectors</strong>, <strong>max 75%</strong> per sector</td>\n<td><strong>Weekly or less often</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hybrid Long-Short</td>\n<td>Hybrid (interval)</td>\n<td><strong>≥25% each</strong> in equity and debt</td>\n<td><strong>Twice a week or less often</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Industry growth</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Measure</th>\n<th>Then</th>\n<th>Now</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Industry AUM</td>\n<td><strong>Rs 11.89 lakh cr</strong> (Mar 2015)</td>\n<td><strong>Rs 82.03 lakh cr</strong> (Feb 2026), <strong>19.3% p.a.</strong> over 11 years</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Folios</td>\n<td><strong>4.8 cr</strong> (Mar 2010)</td>\n<td><strong>27.39 cr</strong> (Mar 2026)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Monthly SIP flow</td>\n<td><strong>Rs 8,055 cr</strong> (Mar 2019)</td>\n<td><strong>Rs 32,087 cr</strong> (Mar 2026)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIP assets</td>\n<td></td>\n<td><strong>Rs 15.11 lakh cr</strong> (Mar 2026)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MF share of household financial investment</td>\n<td><strong>10%</strong> (2016)</td>\n<td><strong>14%</strong> (2018); bank deposits <strong>71% → 65%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li>Unit capital = units x <strong>face value</strong>; AUM = units x <strong>NAV</strong>.</li>\n<li>Close-ended schemes are compulsorily listed <strong>except ELSS</strong>.</li>\n<li>Credit risk fund: 65% in <strong>AA and below</strong> (AA+ excluded); corporate bond fund: 80% in <strong>AA+ and above</strong>.</li>\n<li>Mid cap = <strong>101-250</strong>, not 101-200; small cap = <strong>251 onwards</strong>, by full market cap.</li>\n<li>Focused fund: max <strong>30</strong> stocks, not 20, with 80% equity.</li>\n<li>Large cap, dividend yield, value, contra, sectoral, thematic: <strong>80%</strong>; mid cap, small cap and flexi cap: <strong>65%</strong>.</li>\n<li>ELSS: <strong>80%</strong> equity, not 65%, with a <strong>3-year</strong> lock-in; 80C deduction in the <strong>Old</strong> Tax Regime only.</li>\n<li>Index funds, ETFs and FoFs: <strong>95%</strong>, not 80%.</li>\n<li>Ultra-Short-Term = <strong>3-6 months</strong>; Ultra Short to Short Term (old low duration) = <strong>6-12 months</strong>.</li>\n<li>Balanced Advantage = <strong>dynamic</strong> equity/debt; Balanced Hybrid = 40-60% equity with <strong>no arbitrage</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-b (NAV), 2-c (economies of scale), 3-c (close-ended), 4-c (no limit if overlap &lt;50%), 5-b (equity down, debt up).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch3", "n": 3, "title": "Legal Structure of Mutual Funds", "marks": 4, "html": "<ul>\n<li>MF definition: a fund set up as a <strong>trust</strong>, <strong>granted registration under Regulation 3</strong>, raising money by selling <strong>units</strong> to the public under <strong>schemes</strong>, to invest in securities, money market, <strong>gold, silver</strong> and other assets SEBI specifies.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Legal basis</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Governed by</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Governing regulation</td>\n<td><strong>SEBI (Mutual Funds) Regulations, 2026</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trust</td>\n<td><strong>Indian Trusts Act, 1882</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trust deed registration</td>\n<td><strong>Indian Registration Act, 1908</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Who creates or appoints whom</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Entity</th>\n<th>Created / appointed by</th>\n<th>Note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Trust</td>\n<td><strong>Sponsor</strong> creates it</td>\n<td><strong>beneficiaries = unitholders</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AMC</td>\n<td><strong>sponsor or trustees</strong></td>\n<td>With <strong>SEBI approval</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Custodian</strong></td>\n<td><strong>trustees</strong></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>RTA</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AMC</strong></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Collecting banker</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AMC</strong></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Scheme auditor</strong></td>\n<td><strong>trustees</strong></td>\n<td>Must <strong>differ</strong> from the <strong>AMC auditor</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AMC auditor</td>\n<td>The AMC</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Key agreements</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Document</th>\n<th>Between</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Trust deed</strong></td>\n<td>Executed between <strong>sponsor and trustees</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Investment Management Agreement</strong></td>\n<td>Trustees sign it with the AMC</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Sponsor</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Role</td>\n<td><strong>Sponsor applies</strong> to SEBI for MF registration and invests in the <strong>AMC's capital</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Experience</td>\n<td><strong>5 years</strong> in financial services</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Net worth</td>\n<td><strong>positive net worth</strong> in each of the last <strong>5 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Profit</td>\n<td><strong>net profit</strong> in each of the last <strong>5 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Average profit</td>\n<td><strong>≥ Rs 10 crore</strong> over 5 years</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Liquid net worth</strong></td>\n<td>Must exceed the sponsor's proposed <strong>capital contribution</strong> to the AMC</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Trustees</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Form</td>\n<td>Individuals (<strong>Board of Trustees</strong>) or a <strong>trustee company</strong> (acts through its Board of Directors)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Eligibility (<strong>Regulation 11</strong>)</td>\n<td><strong>fit and proper</strong> (Schedule II, Intermediaries Regulations 2008); <strong>not a director, officer or employee of an AMC</strong>; <strong>not trustee of another MF</strong>; furnishes information SEBI asks for</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Appointment</td>\n<td>Needs <strong>prior SEBI approval</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Independence</td>\n<td>At least <strong>two-thirds</strong> of the trustee board = <strong>independent directors</strong> (not associates of the sponsor, AMC or trustee company)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Trustee duties (6 heads)</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Duty head</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td><strong>appoint/terminate the AMC</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><strong>conflicts of interest and broker empanelment</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><strong>regulatory compliance</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><strong>oversight for investor interests</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td><strong>additional oversight</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Due diligence on matters SEBI specifies</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>AMC</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Directors</td>\n<td><strong>professional experience</strong> in finance; directors and key personnel must be <strong>fit and proper</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Independence</td>\n<td>At least <strong>50%</strong> of AMC directors must <strong>not be associates</strong> of the sponsor, its subsidiaries or the trustees</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Board limits</td>\n<td>AMC directors (<strong>incl. Chairman</strong>) can't sit on the board of <strong>any MF's trustee company</strong>; no one can be a director of <strong>more than one AMC</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Director appointment</td>\n<td>Needs <strong>prior trustee approval</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Net worth</td>\n<td><strong>≥ Rs 50 crore</strong> (from <strong>1 Jan 2024</strong>); maintained <strong>continuously</strong>; <strong>sponsor's responsibility</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change of control</td>\n<td>Needs <strong>prior approval of trustees and SEBI</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>On change of control</td>\n<td>Letter to each unitholder; ad in <strong>1 English national daily + 1 regional-language paper</strong>; <strong>exit at NAV with no exit load for ≥30 calendar days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Removal</td>\n<td>By <strong>majority of trustees</strong> or <strong>75% of unitholders</strong>; any change needs <strong>SEBI + unitholder approval</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Custodian</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Registration</td>\n<td>Under <strong>SEBI (Custodian) Regulations, 1996</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Independence</td>\n<td>Can't be one where the sponsor holds <strong>≥50% voting rights</strong> or <strong>≥50% of directors</strong>, unless conditions are met</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Role</td>\n<td><strong>Custodian tracks corporate actions</strong> (dividends, bonus, rights) and settles trades</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Compliance, fund management, accounting and risk</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Role</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Compliance Officer</strong></td>\n<td>Signs the <strong>due-diligence certificate</strong> on new scheme documents; reports to the <strong>AMC head</strong>; flags non-compliance <strong>directly to trustees</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fund management: <strong>analysts</strong></td>\n<td>Find ideas</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fund management: <strong>fund managers</strong></td>\n<td>Own scheme performance</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fund management: <strong>dealers</strong></td>\n<td>Place orders</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Fund accounting</strong> team</td>\n<td>Calculates NAV <strong>daily</strong>; separate from the AMC's <strong>accounts</strong> team</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Risk officers</td>\n<td>SEBI <strong>Risk Management Framework</strong>: dedicated officers for <strong>investment, compliance, operational, cyber</strong> risk</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Other entities</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Who</th>\n<th>Key rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Fund accountant</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No SEBI registration</strong> needed; can be in-house</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>RTA</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Must register with SEBI</strong>, but appointing one is <strong>optional</strong>; its offices act as <strong>ISCs</strong> (Investor Service Centres)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MFD</td>\n<td><strong>NISM V-A + AMFI registration</strong>; the limited-scheme cadre needs <strong>NISM V-B</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>KRAs</strong></td>\n<td>SEBI regulations in <strong>2011</strong>; one KYC across the securities market, under <strong>PMLA</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Valuation agencies</td>\n<td>Fair valuation of non-traded debt uses <strong>≥2 valuation agencies</strong>: <strong>CRISIL and ICRA</strong>, appointed by AMFI; AMCs use their <strong>valuation level</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Depositories</td>\n<td><strong>NSDL and CDSL</strong>; investors deal through <strong>DPs</strong> (like bank branches)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>FMP</strong>: may disclose <strong>proposed rating profile</strong> before investing; can then invest only <strong>at that rating or safer</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>ETF units must be in demat</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Transaction platforms</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Platform</th>\n<th>Key point</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Exchange platforms</td>\n<td><strong>BSE StAR MF</strong> and <strong>NSE NMF-II</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MF Utilities</strong></td>\n<td>An <strong>AMFI industry</strong> platform</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Execution Only Platform</strong></td>\n<td>Only for <strong>direct plans</strong>; RIA and broker platforms for their own clients are <strong>not EOPs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>EOP Category 1</strong></td>\n<td>Registers with <strong>AMFI</strong>; body corporate; <strong>agent of AMCs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>EOP Category 2</strong></td>\n<td>Registers as a <strong>stock broker</strong> in the exchange EOP segment; <strong>agent of investor</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>AMFI</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>What it is</td>\n<td><strong>AMFI</strong> = association of all AMCs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Powers</td>\n<td>Issues <strong>ARN</strong>; can <strong>cancel ARN</strong> for code violations</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Status</td>\n<td><strong>AMFI is neither a regulator nor an SRO</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li>Custodian is appointed by the <strong>trustees</strong>, not the AMC; the RTA and collecting banker are appointed by the <strong>AMC</strong>.</li>\n<li>Trust deed is between the <strong>sponsor and trustees</strong>; the Investment Management Agreement is between the <strong>trustees and AMC</strong>.</li>\n<li>Sponsor eligibility uses <strong>5 years</strong> throughout (experience, net worth, profit), with average profit <strong>≥ Rs 10 crore</strong>.</li>\n<li>Trustee board: <strong>two-thirds</strong> independent; AMC board: <strong>50%</strong> non-associate.</li>\n<li>AMC net worth <strong>≥ Rs 50 crore</strong>, maintained continuously, is the <strong>sponsor's</strong> responsibility.</li>\n<li>AMC removal: <strong>majority of trustees</strong> or <strong>75% of unitholders</strong>; any change needs SEBI + unitholder approval.</li>\n<li>Fund accountant needs <strong>no SEBI registration</strong>; the RTA <strong>must register</strong> with SEBI but appointing one is <strong>optional</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>AMFI</strong> is neither a regulator nor an SRO; CRISIL and ICRA are appointed by <strong>AMFI</strong>, not SEBI.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-c (unitholders), 2-b (custodian), 3-a (association of AMCs), 4-c (CRISIL and ICRA), 5-a (AMC).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch4", "n": 4, "title": "Legal and Regulatory Framework", "marks": 10, "html": "<h3>Regulators and SEBI</h3>\n<h4>The four regulators</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Regulator</th>\n<th>Regulates</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>RBI</td>\n<td>Banks, money market</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SEBI</td>\n<td>Securities</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>IRDAI</td>\n<td>Insurance</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PFRDA</td>\n<td>Pension</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>All 4 are under the <strong>Ministry of Finance</strong>.</li>\n<li>RBI rules also apply to MFs for <strong>money market, overseas investment, forex</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>SEBI and MF regulation</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Who regulates MFs</td>\n<td><strong>SEBI regulates mutual funds</strong>; <strong>AMFI does not</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MF regulations</td>\n<td>First issued in <strong>1996</strong>, now replaced by the <strong>MF Regulations 2026</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\"Securities\"</td>\n<td>Transferable, tradeable instruments, defined in <strong>Sec 2(h) of the SCRA, 1956</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SEBI preamble</td>\n<td><strong>Protect investors, develop and regulate</strong> the securities market</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Benchmarks, risk class and crisis reforms</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Benchmark</td>\n<td><strong>Total Return Index (TRI)</strong>, which includes dividends and interest; not a <strong>Price Return Index</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PRC matrix (debt schemes)</td>\n<td><strong>Potential Risk Class (PRC) matrix</strong>: <strong>Macaulay duration</strong> × <strong>Credit Risk Value</strong>; effective <strong>1 Dec 2021</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Segregated portfolio</td>\n<td>Separates distressed assets after a <strong>credit event</strong>; introduced <strong>after</strong> the <strong>2018</strong> credit crisis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>2008</strong> crisis reforms</td>\n<td><strong>No premature redemption in FMPs</strong>; <strong>\"liquid plus\"</strong> name banned</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Investment restrictions</h3>\n<h4>What an MF can invest in</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rule</th>\n<th>What it says</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Regulation 39</strong></td>\n<td>MF may invest <strong>only</strong> in securities, money market instruments, <strong>privately placed debentures</strong>, <strong>securitised debt</strong> (asset or mortgage backed), <strong>gold</strong>, <strong>silver</strong> and anything else SEBI specifies</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sixth Schedule</strong></td>\n<td>Equity and debt only if <strong>listed or to be listed</strong>, except <strong>unlisted G-secs and money market instruments (not CPs)</strong> and <strong>unlisted NCDs</strong> as SEBI allows; <strong>unrated debt</strong> on SEBI's conditions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SIF</strong> (<strong>Regulation 51</strong>)</td>\n<td>Same permitted instruments as MFs (Reg 39); the <strong>Sixth Schedule</strong> restrictions apply</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Regulation 41</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Area</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>All investments</td>\n<td>Follow the <strong>Sixth Schedule</strong> (except <strong>gold and silver ETFs</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Settlement</td>\n<td><strong>Only in demat</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carry-forward</td>\n<td><strong>No carry-forward</strong> deals except as SEBI allows</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Derivatives and <strong>short selling</strong></td>\n<td>Only on a <strong>recognised stock exchange</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Inter-scheme transfers</strong></td>\n<td>Only on SEBI's conditions</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Other investment rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gold/silver ETFs</strong></td>\n<td>Invest <strong>only in gold/silver</strong> (or related instruments), except for <strong>redemption liquidity</strong>; may use <strong>exchange-traded commodity derivatives</strong>; idle money in <strong>short-term bank deposits</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scheme into <strong>another MF scheme</strong></td>\n<td>Allowed with <strong>no fees</strong> (not for FoFs)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Investing in a FoF</td>\n<td><strong>No scheme can invest in a FoF</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>FoF</td>\n<td><strong>Can't invest in another FoF</strong>; holds <strong>only MF units</strong> (plus liquidity)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trades</td>\n<td><strong>Delivery basis</strong> only (short selling and derivatives allowed under SEBI's framework)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Holding</td>\n<td>Securities held <strong>in the MF's name</strong> for the scheme</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Money awaiting deployment</td>\n<td>Can sit in <strong>short-term deposits of scheduled commercial banks</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Limits</td>\n<td>All investments follow SEBI's <strong>prudential limits</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Advertisement code</h3>\n<h4>Ad rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Banned</td>\n<td><strong>No testimonials, no rankings, no celebrities, no projections</strong>; no unfair comparisons</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Standard warning</td>\n<td>\"<strong>Mutual Fund investments are subject to market risks, read all scheme related documents carefully.</strong>\" <strong>No words added or removed</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Audio-visual</td>\n<td>The <strong>14-word</strong> warning, visual + voice-over, <strong>at least 5 seconds</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vernacular ads</td>\n<td>Warning <strong>in the vernacular</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Where the rules sit</td>\n<td><strong>Fifth Schedule</strong> of the MF Regulations 2026</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>IDCW ads</td>\n<td><strong>Rs per unit + face value + prevailing NAV</strong>; state <strong>just below the payout figure</strong> that NAV will <strong>fall by the payout and statutory levy</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Celebrity endorsement</td>\n<td><strong>Industry level only</strong>, <strong>prior SEBI approval</strong>, paid from the <strong>investor education</strong> pool; <strong>not</strong> for a scheme or AMC brand</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unverified market news</td>\n<td>Forward only after the <strong>Compliance Officer's</strong> approval</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Performance in ads</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scheme</th>\n<th>What to show</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Overnight, liquid, money market</td>\n<td><strong>Simple annualised</strong> yield allowed if data for <strong>7, 15 and 30 days</strong> exists</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scheme <strong>&gt;3 years</strong></td>\n<td>CAGR for <strong>1, 3, 5 years and since inception</strong> (since <strong>allotment date</strong>) + <strong>point-to-point on Rs 10,000</strong>; say <strong>regular or direct</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&lt;6 months</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No</strong> performance</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>6–12 months</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Simple annualised</strong> 6-month return</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other schemes of the <strong>same fund manager</strong></td>\n<td>Show all (CAGR 1/3/5 yrs); <strong>&gt;6 schemes</strong>: count + <strong>top 3 and bottom 3</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Additional benchmark</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scheme type</th>\n<th>Additional benchmark</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity, balanced, aggressive, BAF, multi-asset, retirement, children's</td>\n<td><strong>Sensex/Nifty</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt ≤1 yr + <strong>arbitrage</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1-yr T-bill</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other debt, <strong>conservative hybrid, equity savings</strong></td>\n<td><strong>10-yr GoI</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>SIF advertising and branding</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Identity</td>\n<td>Needs a <strong>distinct brand, logo, website/page</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MF brand</td>\n<td>Allowed for <strong>5 years</strong> from SEBI approval, with phrases like <strong>\"brought to you by\"</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Font</td>\n<td>The MF brand's font must be <strong>no bigger</strong> than the SIF's</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ad rules</td>\n<td>MF ad rules apply</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Investor rights</h3>\n<h4>Unitholder rights</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Right</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Ownership</td>\n<td>Proportionate <strong>beneficial ownership</strong>; can ask for a <strong>unit certificate</strong> or <strong>demat</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Transfer</td>\n<td>Demat units <strong>freely transferable</strong> (<strong>except ELSS</strong> in lock-in)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change distributor</td>\n<td>Switch distributor or go direct by <strong>written request</strong>; <strong>no NOC</strong> needed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Inspect</td>\n<td><strong>Trust Deed, IMA, Custodial agreement, RTA agreement, AMC Memorandum &amp; Articles</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Nomination</td>\n<td><strong>Up to 10 nominees</strong>; no % given = <strong>equal split</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pledge</td>\n<td>Can <strong>pledge</strong> units</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Accountability and remedies</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Complaint status</td>\n<td>Goes in the <strong>annual report</strong>, MF site and <strong>AMFI site</strong>; pending complaints can <strong>block new scheme launches</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change in <strong>fundamental attributes</strong> (or fees)</td>\n<td><strong>Written communication</strong> to each unitholder (<strong>email/SMS allowed</strong>) + details on the <strong>AMC website</strong> + <strong>exit at NAV with no load</strong>, window <strong>≥30 days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>75% of unitholders</strong></td>\n<td>Can <strong>remove the AMC</strong> or <strong>wind up</strong> a scheme</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Legal action</td>\n<td>Sue the <strong>trustees</strong> for breach of trust, <strong>not the trust</strong> (a notional entity)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Caveat emptor</strong></td>\n<td>Applies; a <strong>prospective investor</strong> has no such rights</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Unclaimed money, debt trades and recoveries</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Situation</th>\n<th>Treatment</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Unclaimed money <strong>within 3 yrs</strong></td>\n<td>Paid at <strong>prevailing NAV</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unclaimed money <strong>after 3 yrs</strong></td>\n<td>Paid at <strong>NAV at end of year 3</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Where unclaimed amounts go</td>\n<td>A <strong>separate liquid plan</strong>; max fee <strong>0.50% p.a.</strong>; <strong>no exit load</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt trades</td>\n<td>Disclosed <strong>daily</strong>, with a <strong>15-day lag</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Illiquid security recovered later</td>\n<td>Substantial and <strong>within 2 yrs</strong>: goes to <strong>old investors</strong>; otherwise to the <strong>Investor Education Fund</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Grievances and codes</h3>\n<h4>Grievances and oversight</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>AMC complaint resolution</td>\n<td>Within <strong>21 calendar days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SCORES</strong></td>\n<td>SEBI's online complaints system; physical complaints get <strong>scanned and uploaded</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cyber framework <strong>CSCRF</strong></td>\n<td>Goals (from <strong>CERT-In</strong>): <strong>Anticipate, Withstand, Contain, Recover, Evolve</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Distributor checks</td>\n<td>AMCs do <strong>due diligence</strong> on distributors; <strong>AMFI</strong> often runs a <strong>common</strong> process</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Codes of conduct</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Code</th>\n<th>Covers</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Fourth Schedule</strong></td>\n<td>SEBI code of conduct for <strong>AMCs and trustees</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>AMFI Code of Ethics (ACE)</strong></td>\n<td>Sets <strong>higher, more explicit</strong> standards</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>AGNI</strong></td>\n<td>AMFI Guidelines &amp; Norms for <strong>Intermediaries</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Breach process</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Step</th>\n<th>What happens</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Explanation within <strong>3 weeks</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><strong>Warning letter</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><strong>2nd proven violation = ARN cancelled</strong>, all AMCs told</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Appeal</td>\n<td><strong>Appeal to AMFI</strong> allowed</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>MFD code (Appendix 3)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>MFD acts as a <strong>fiduciary</strong>: <strong>investor's interest is paramount</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>MFD code rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Area</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Inducements</td>\n<td><strong>No rebates or pass-back</strong>, no gifts or inducements</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Transactions</td>\n<td><strong>No churning</strong>, <strong>no splitting applications</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Disclosure</td>\n<td>Disclose <strong>all commissions</strong> across competing schemes and <strong>group/affiliate conflicts</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Direct plans</td>\n<td>MFDs <strong>cannot deal in direct plans</strong>; platforms must say <strong>regular plan with commission</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Returns</td>\n<td><strong>No indicative portfolio, yield or assured returns</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Client forms</td>\n<td>Never enter the <strong>MFD's own contact details</strong> on a client form; always add the <strong>EUIN</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Marketing material</td>\n<td>Use <strong>AMC-provided marketing material</strong> only; no AMC logo without <strong>written approval</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Suitability</td>\n<td>Ask about <strong>financial status, experience, objectives</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Client data</td>\n<td>Don't share with <strong>group companies for cross-selling</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sub-distributors</td>\n<td>Must hold a <strong>valid ARN</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Clawback</td>\n<td><strong>Refund clawback</strong> commissions to AMCs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Representative misconduct</td>\n<td>Report a Representative's <strong>moral turpitude or arrest</strong> to the <strong>AMC and AMFI</strong> immediately</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Titles</td>\n<td>Can't call yourself <strong>adviser, wealth manager or consultant</strong> unless a <strong>SEBI RIA</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tagline</td>\n<td><strong>\"AMFI-registered Mutual Fund Distributor\"</strong>, font <strong>≥12</strong> in print</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li>Ad rules are in the <strong>Fifth Schedule</strong>; code of conduct for AMCs and trustees is the <strong>Fourth</strong>; investment restrictions are the <strong>Sixth</strong>.</li>\n<li>AMC resolves complaints within <strong>21 calendar days</strong>, not 30.</li>\n<li>Unclaimed money: within 3 years at <strong>prevailing NAV</strong>; after 3 years at the <strong>NAV at the end of year 3</strong>; liquid plan fee cap <strong>0.50%</strong>, not 1%.</li>\n<li>Celebrity endorsement is <strong>industry-level only</strong>, with prior SEBI approval, paid from the <strong>investor education</strong> pool; never for a scheme or AMC brand.</li>\n<li>Sue the <strong>trustees</strong> for breach of trust, not the trust (a notional entity).</li>\n<li>Ad performance: under 6 months <strong>none</strong>; 6 to 12 months <strong>simple annualised</strong> 6-month return, not CAGR.</li>\n<li>Additional benchmark: arbitrage and debt up to 1 year = <strong>1-yr T-bill</strong>; conservative hybrid and equity savings = <strong>10-yr GoI</strong>, not Sensex/Nifty.</li>\n<li>AGNI is for <strong>intermediaries</strong>; the Fourth Schedule code is for <strong>AMCs and trustees</strong>.</li>\n<li>Gold and silver ETFs are <strong>exempt</strong> from the Sixth Schedule; every other investment follows it.</li>\n<li>2008 reform banned the name <strong>\"liquid plus\"</strong>, not \"liquid\"; segregated portfolios came after the <strong>2018</strong> crisis; PRC uses <strong>Macaulay</strong> duration.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-a (SEBI), 2-a (True), 3-a (industry-level celebrity), 4-d (ten).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch5", "n": 5, "title": "Scheme Related Information", "marks": 10, "html": "<h3>Mandatory documents</h3>\n<h4>The documents</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Document</th>\n<th>What it is</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Scheme related documents</strong></td>\n<td><strong>SID + SAI</strong> (+ <strong>KIM</strong>); the standard warning refers to these</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SID</strong></td>\n<td>Details of <strong>one scheme</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SAI</strong></td>\n<td>Statutory info on the <strong>MF/AMC</strong>; <strong>one SAI for all schemes</strong>; legally <strong>SAI is part of the SID</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Caveat emptor</strong>: the investor is <strong>presumed to have read</strong> them; signing the form is <strong>legal acceptance</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Format, SEBI's role and publication</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Format</td>\n<td><strong>Prescribed by SEBI</strong>; content in the <strong>same sequence</strong>; MF may add other <strong>material</strong> disclosures</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SEBI's role</td>\n<td>SEBI <strong>does not approve</strong>, it gives <strong>observations</strong>; documents are <strong>vetted</strong>, not approved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Where published</td>\n<td><strong>Drafts</strong> on <strong>SEBI's</strong> website; <strong>final</strong> documents on <strong>AMFI's</strong> website and the MF's own site</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Offer to contract</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Stage</th>\n<th>What it is</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Offer</td>\n<td>The documents</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Acceptance</strong></td>\n<td>Signed form + payment</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Contract completes</strong></td>\n<td>On unit allotment</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>What sits where</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Where / content</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>SID cover page</td>\n<td>Name, type (open/close/interval), <strong>face value</strong>, NFO dates, AMC and trustee details</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cover disclaimer</td>\n<td>Filed with SEBI with an AMC <strong>Due Diligence Certificate</strong>; <strong>SEBI has not approved or certified</strong> it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Risk-o-meter and suitability statement</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Front page of the SID</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Standard risk</td>\n<td><strong>Sponsor not liable</strong> beyond its <strong>initial contribution</strong>; <strong>past performance not indicative</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Eligible and ineligible investors</strong></td>\n<td>SID's <strong>NFO and Ongoing Offer</strong> section</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Investment objective</td>\n<td>Can be <strong>primary + secondary</strong>; also shown in <strong>Highlights</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>How to apply</strong> (PAN, KYC, payment modes, third-party rules, cut-off, minors, NRIs)</td>\n<td><strong>SAI</strong>, read with SID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Modes of transaction</strong></td>\n<td>SAI's <strong>\"How to Apply\"</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fees</strong> hit the <strong>NAV</strong>; <strong>loads</strong> are paid <strong>by the investor</strong> at exit.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fundamental attributes</h3>\n<h4>The three fundamental attributes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Attribute</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>(i)</td>\n<td><strong>Type of scheme</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(ii)</td>\n<td><strong>Investment objective</strong> + <strong>min/max asset allocation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(iii)</td>\n<td><strong>Terms of issue</strong>: liquidity, <strong>aggregate fees and expenses</strong>, <strong>any safety net or guarantee</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>To change them (<strong>Regulation 22(9)(c)</strong>): <strong>written communication</strong> to each unitholder (<strong>email/SMS allowed</strong>) + details on the <strong>AMC website</strong> + <strong>exit at prevailing NAV with no exit load</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>SAI and KIM</h3>\n<h4>SAI, KIM and addendum</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SAI</strong> contents</td>\n<td>Constituents (sponsor, AMC, trustee, custodian, RTA, auditor, fund accountant if outsourced, bankers), <strong>condensed financials</strong> for schemes of the <strong>last 3 FYs</strong>, <strong>valuation norms</strong>, nomination, transmission, minors, pledge, tax, grievances</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SAI access</td>\n<td>Investors can ask for a <strong>printed SAI</strong>; all SAIs on <strong>AMFI's</strong> site</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>KIM</strong></td>\n<td>Summary of <strong>SID + SAI</strong>; <strong>every application form must carry a KIM</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>KIM performance</td>\n<td><strong>1, 3, 5 years and since inception</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Addendum</strong></td>\n<td>Interim change; it is <strong>part of the documents</strong> and <strong>must go with the KIM</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Update timelines</h3>\n<h4>When documents are updated</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Document / event</th>\n<th>Timeline</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SID</strong></td>\n<td>First update within <strong>6 months</strong> of the half-year of launch; then within <strong>1 month of each half-year</strong> (<strong>Sept and March</strong> data)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change in fundamental attributes</td>\n<td><strong>Addendum immediately</strong>; SID revised <strong>after the exit window</strong> (≥30 days); public notice</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other changes</td>\n<td><strong>Addendum</strong> on website and to <strong>distributors and ISCs</strong>, attached to KIM/SID stock; <strong>account statements show the load structure</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SAI</strong></td>\n<td>Within <strong>3 months of FY end</strong>; material changes <strong>ongoing</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>KIM</strong></td>\n<td>At least <strong>once every half-year</strong>, within <strong>1 month</strong>; filed with SEBI <strong>electronically</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Other disclosures</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Current value = <strong>units × NAV</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>NAV disclosure</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scheme</th>\n<th>NAV declared</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>NAV (general rule)</td>\n<td><strong>Every business day</strong>, on the <strong>AMC and AMFI</strong> sites</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Liquid and overnight</strong></td>\n<td>Also for <strong>Sundays and holidays</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Close-ended</td>\n<td><strong>At least weekly</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Expenses and TER</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Expense disclosure</td>\n<td>Trustees and AMCs ensure every expense is <strong>identified and disclosed</strong> in the offer document and within the Regulations</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>TER</strong> disclosure</td>\n<td><strong>Daily</strong> on the AMC and AMFI sites (<strong>all schemes except IDFs</strong>), in <strong>Format 7E</strong>, downloadable and <strong>machine-readable</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Large expense items</td>\n<td>Any expense item <strong>&gt;10% of total expenditure</strong> is disclosed in the scheme accounts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TER formula</td>\n<td><strong>TER = Base Expense Ratio (BER) + brokerage + transaction cost + statutory levies (incl. GST)</strong>; BER under <strong>Regulation 66(7)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Direct plan BER</td>\n<td><strong>Lower</strong> (no distribution cost, <strong>no commission</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Any change in BER</strong></td>\n<td>Email/SMS and website <strong>≥3 working days before</strong> it takes effect (effective 8 Jan 2026 = notice by <strong>2 Jan</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Scheme dashboard</strong></td>\n<td>On the AMC site: AUM, TER, fund manager, benchmark, exit load, portfolio, performance</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Risk-o-meter: 6 levels</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>Colour</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td><strong>Irish Green</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Low to Moderate</td>\n<td><strong>Chartreuse</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Moderate</td>\n<td><strong>Neon Yellow</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Moderately High</td>\n<td><strong>Caramel</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>High</td>\n<td><strong>Dark Orange</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Very High</td>\n<td><strong>Red</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Risk-o-meter and SIF Risk-Band rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Risk-o-meter review</td>\n<td><strong>Monthly</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Risk-o-meter change</td>\n<td><strong>Notice-cum-addendum + email/SMS</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Display</td>\n<td>Show the <strong>scheme and benchmark</strong> risk-o-meter together</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Use</td>\n<td>Only the <strong>first step</strong>, not the sole basis for decisions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SIF Risk-Band</strong></td>\n<td><strong>5 levels</strong>; set at <strong>NFO</strong>; reviewed <strong>monthly</strong>; published within <strong>10 days</strong>; <strong>31 March</strong> level + number of changes on AMC and AMFI sites</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Commodity risk score</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Annualised volatility</th>\n<th>Score</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&lt;10%</strong></td>\n<td><strong>3</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>10–15%</strong></td>\n<td><strong>4</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>15–20%</strong></td>\n<td><strong>5</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt;20%</strong></td>\n<td><strong>6</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Score is from <strong>annualised volatility</strong>, reviewed <strong>quarterly</strong> on <strong>15 years</strong> of prices.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Periodic disclosures</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Disclosure</th>\n<th>How often / when</th>\n<th>Where / notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Portfolio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Monthly and half-yearly</strong>, within <strong>10 days</strong></td>\n<td>With <strong>ISIN</strong>; AMC and AMFI sites</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Debt schemes</strong> portfolio</td>\n<td><strong>Fortnightly</strong>, within <strong>5 days</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Plus yield</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SIF portfolio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Every alternate month</strong> (May, Jul, Sep, Nov, Jan, Mar), within <strong>10 days</strong></td>\n<td>SIF <strong>ISID</strong> must include <strong>scenario analysis</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Unaudited half-yearly results</strong></td>\n<td>Within <strong>1 month</strong> of 31 March / 30 Sept</td>\n<td>Hosted on the website, in SEBI's format; unitholders told by <strong>written communication (email/SMS)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Annual report</strong></td>\n<td>Within <strong>4 months</strong> of FY end</td>\n<td>Ad in <strong>English + Hindi</strong> national dailies; <strong>functional link</strong> to scheme-wise annual reports on the website</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Factsheet</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Not mandatory</strong> (voluntary); publishing it <strong>monthly</strong> is an <strong>AMFI best practice</strong></td>\n<td>SEBI disclosure rules still apply; shows PE, beta, SD, Sharpe, rating profile, maturity, duration</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>MFs may use derivatives <strong>to hedge</strong>, but <strong>can't take open derivative positions</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li>SEBI gives <strong>observations</strong> on the SID; it does <strong>not approve</strong> or certify it (documents are vetted, not approved).</li>\n<li><strong>One SAI</strong> serves all schemes of a fund; the <strong>SID</strong> is per scheme; legally the SAI is part of the SID.</li>\n<li>Drafts go on <strong>SEBI's</strong> website; final documents on <strong>AMFI's</strong> website and the MF's own site.</li>\n<li>Risk-o-meter is reviewed <strong>monthly</strong>; commodity risk score is reviewed <strong>quarterly</strong> on <strong>15 years</strong> of prices.</li>\n<li>SAI update: within <strong>3 months</strong> of FY end; SID and KIM: within <strong>1 month</strong> of each half-year.</li>\n<li>Annual report within <strong>4 months</strong> of FY end; unaudited half-yearly results within <strong>1 month</strong>.</li>\n<li>Debt portfolio: <strong>fortnightly, within 5 days</strong>, plus yield; all schemes: monthly and half-yearly within <strong>10 days</strong>.</li>\n<li>Low = <strong>Irish Green</strong>, Low to Moderate = <strong>Chartreuse</strong>, Moderate = Neon Yellow, Moderately High = <strong>Caramel</strong>, High = Dark Orange, Very High = Red.</li>\n<li>Factsheet is <strong>voluntary</strong>; monthly publication is an <strong>AMFI best practice</strong>, not a SEBI mandate.</li>\n<li><strong>Fees</strong> hit the NAV; <strong>loads</strong> are paid by the investor at exit. BER change needs <strong>3 working days'</strong> notice; BER sits under <strong>Regulation 66(7)</strong>, not 22(9)(c).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-d (SID + SAI), 2-c (SEBI format), 3-b (six months), 4-b (AMC), 5-a (factsheet).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch6", "n": 6, "title": "Fund Distribution and Channel Management", "marks": 6, "html": "<h4>Who analyses what</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Who</th>\n<th>Analyses</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Distributor</strong></td>\n<td>the <strong>investor</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Fund manager</strong></td>\n<td>the <strong>market</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Channels: individuals, banks, national/regional distributors, NBFCs, brokers, <strong>post offices</strong>, direct, online/<strong>e-commerce</strong>.</li>\n<li>Paper forms go to <strong>OPOAs</strong> (Official Points of Acceptance).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Distribution models and players</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Model / player</th>\n<th>Key point</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>LIC and UTI</strong></td>\n<td>Built the <strong>individual agent</strong> force</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Employee model</td>\n<td><strong>Fixed costs</strong> (salary)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sub-agent model</td>\n<td><strong>Variable costs</strong> (commission)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Multinational banks</strong></td>\n<td>Entered MF distribution <strong>first</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PSU banks</td>\n<td>Give <strong>non-urban reach</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Distribution companies and banks</strong></td>\n<td>= <strong>institutional distributors</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Stock exchange platforms</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Platforms</td>\n<td><strong>NSE NMF-II</strong>, <strong>BSE StAR MF</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Who can use</td>\n<td>Only <strong>AMFI-registered</strong> trading members who have signed up with the MF</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DPs</td>\n<td><strong>Can only process redemptions</strong> on exchange platforms</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Listing</td>\n<td>Eligible open-ended schemes are <strong>not listed</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AMFI-registered distributors</td>\n<td>Can take <strong>limited purpose membership</strong> of an exchange</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Role of exchange</td>\n<td><strong>Order-routing</strong> system; <strong>don't replace RTAs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Settlement</td>\n<td><strong>No settlement guarantee</strong> (the <strong>AMC</strong> is responsible)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Grievances</td>\n<td>Exchange grievance redressal still applies</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Investors</td>\n<td>May <strong>directly</strong> use exchange infrastructure (SEBI circular, <strong>26 Feb 2020</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Transactions</td>\n<td>SIP, STP, SWP and switch all work; units credited to <strong>demat</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Other transaction platforms</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Platform</th>\n<th>Key points</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MF Utilities</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CAN</strong> (Common Account Number) needs <strong>KYC</strong>; <strong>one form, one payment</strong> for multiple schemes; <strong>MFU bank/nomination details override folio details</strong>; an investor can have <strong>multiple CANs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>RTA interoperable platform</strong></td>\n<td>Live since <strong>31 Dec 2021</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MFCentral</strong></td>\n<td>Single-window portal built by <strong>CAMS and KFintech</strong> under SEBI mandate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New-age platforms (<strong>Groww, Kuvera, Paytm Money, Coin</strong>)</td>\n<td>Sell <strong>direct plans</strong> too</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>MFCentral: what it offers</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Feature</th>\n<th>Covers</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Consolidated view</strong></td>\n<td>Demat and non-demat folios</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Service requests</strong></td>\n<td>Bank, email/mobile, KYC, nominee</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Transactions</strong></td>\n<td>Lump sum, SIP, redemption, switch</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other</td>\n<td>Folio consolidation, <strong>CAS</strong>, unclaimed amounts, <strong>family portfolio</strong> tracking</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Distributor registration</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Certification</td>\n<td>Must hold <strong>NISM V-A</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Exemption via <strong>CPE</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Age ≥50</strong> or <strong>≥10 yrs</strong> experience <strong>as of 31 May 2010</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>KYD</strong></td>\n<td>PAN + address proof at <strong>CAMS PoS</strong>, <strong>right index finger</strong> biometric; send the acknowledgement to all AMCs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New cadre (V-B)</td>\n<td><strong>Exempt from KYD biometrics</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>ARN</strong></td>\n<td>Minimum age <strong>18</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Employees</td>\n<td>Get an <strong>EUIN</strong> under the firm's ARN (<strong>no separate ARN</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ARN/EUIN applications</td>\n<td><strong>Online only</strong> from <strong>1 Oct 2024</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Empanelment</td>\n<td><strong>Compulsory</strong> to earn commission; <strong>no standard form</strong>; AMC can <strong>terminate anytime</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Commission rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Model</td>\n<td><strong>Full trail model only</strong> (SEBI <strong>Master Circular, 20 March 2026</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Not allowed</td>\n<td><strong>No upfront</strong>, <strong>no upfronting of trail</strong>; <strong>monetary only</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Who pays</td>\n<td>Per <strong>Regulation 66(6)</strong> of the MF Regulations 2026 the <strong>AMC pays</strong> distribution costs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Transaction charges withdrawn</strong></td>\n<td>SEBI, <strong>Aug 2025</strong>; earlier applied to subscriptions <strong>&gt;Rs 10,000</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trail basis</td>\n<td>Calculated on <strong>daily net assets</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trail payment</td>\n<td>Paid <strong>monthly or quarterly</strong>, for <strong>as long as the money stays</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Self-investment</td>\n<td><strong>No commission on self-investment</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Daily trail calculation</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Measure</th>\n<th>Formula</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Daily trail</td>\n<td><strong>AUM × rate ÷ 365</strong></td>\n<td>Rs 10 lakh at 1% = <strong>Rs 27.40/day</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Additional commission for new investors</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Additional commission</strong></td>\n<td>For new investors</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Introduced</td>\n<td>SEBI, <strong>Nov 2025</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Who qualifies</td>\n<td><strong>New PAN</strong> from <strong>B-30</strong> cities, or <strong>new women</strong> investors from <strong>Top 30 and B-30</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lump sum</td>\n<td><strong>1%</strong> of the first application, <strong>max Rs 2,000</strong>, if the investor stays <strong>≥1 year</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIP</td>\n<td><strong>1%</strong> of the <strong>first year's</strong> investment, <strong>max Rs 2,000</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Paid from</td>\n<td>The <strong>2 bps</strong> set aside for <strong>investor education</strong>, with <strong>claw back</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>vs trail</td>\n<td><strong>On top of</strong> trail</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Same investor</td>\n<td><strong>No dual incentive</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>GST on commission</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>GST</strong> applies from</td>\n<td><strong>July 2017</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Threshold</td>\n<td><strong>Rs 20 lakh</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Registered distributor</td>\n<td>Invoices and pays GST</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Unregistered</strong> supplier</td>\n<td>The <strong>registered recipient</strong> pays under <strong>reverse charge</strong> (Sec 9(4) CGST, 5(4) IGST)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Commission disclosure and <strong>due diligence</strong> are triggered by <strong>any one</strong> of the thresholds below.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Commission disclosure and due diligence triggers</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Trigger</th>\n<th>Threshold</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Locations</td>\n<td><strong>&gt;20 locations</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AUM (non-institutional)</td>\n<td><strong>&gt;Rs 100 cr AUM</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Commission, industry-wide</td>\n<td><strong>&gt;Rs 1 cr</strong> commission p.a.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Commission from <strong>one AMC</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&gt;Rs 50 lakh</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Disclosure and due diligence</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Yearly disclosure</td>\n<td>Distributor-wise gross and net inflows, average AUM, <strong>AUM/gross inflows</strong>, and whether a <strong>sponsor associate</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Portfolio turnover <strong>&gt;2× industry average</strong></td>\n<td>Triggers <strong>extra due diligence</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Due diligence</strong> checks</td>\n<td>Business model, penalties and suits, associates, and <strong>suitability processes separated from sales</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Advice and transaction types</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>MFD's advice</td>\n<td><strong>Incidental</strong> to distribution, so no RIA registration needed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Titles</td>\n<td>Can't call himself an <strong>adviser or planner</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Transaction types</td>\n<td><strong>Only two</strong>: <strong>advisory</strong> (appropriateness) and <strong>execution only</strong>; <strong>no third category</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Execution only when unsuitable</td>\n<td><strong>Written warning</strong> acknowledged by the investor + <strong>written \"execution only\" confirmation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mis-selling</td>\n<td>Under <strong>PFUTP 2003</strong>: false statements, hiding facts, hiding risks, <strong>no suitability check</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Distributor nomination</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Distributor nomination</strong>: commission</td>\n<td>Goes to the nominee (or legal heir) until the investor changes the ARN or <strong>AUM becomes nil</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Nominee's ARN</td>\n<td><strong>Need not hold an ARN</strong> to receive commission</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Capacity</td>\n<td>Receives it <strong>as trustee for legal heirs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deceased's ARN</td>\n<td>Must be <strong>valid and not suspended on the date of death</strong>; <strong>no new business or SIPs</strong> under it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>AUM transfer</strong> to a nominee</td>\n<td>Needs a <strong>valid ARN + KYD</strong>; the nominee must <strong>inform all clients</strong> by letter or email; investors get <strong>15 days</strong> to object to the AMC</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Change of distributor</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Situation</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Investor changes distributor</td>\n<td><strong>No commission to either</strong> the old or new distributor, <strong>except</strong> when the old distributor <strong>voluntarily ceased business</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Investor-initiated ARN change</td>\n<td>The AMC <strong>may</strong> pay trail to the new distributor after a <strong>12-month cooling-off</strong> period</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Distributor-initiated code change</td>\n<td>Allowed <strong>only</strong> for: change of <strong>name/legal status</strong>, <strong>merger/acquisition within group</strong>, <strong>family AUM consolidation</strong>, <strong>transfer of business</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Conditions (distributor-initiated)</td>\n<td><strong>Entire AUM</strong>, to a <strong>valid KYD ARN</strong>, <strong>old ARN surrendered</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li><strong>Multinational banks</strong> entered MF distribution first; <strong>PSU banks</strong> give non-urban reach.</li>\n<li>On exchanges, <strong>DPs can only process redemptions</strong>; exchanges are order-routing only, <strong>don't replace RTAs</strong>, and the <strong>AMC</strong> (not the exchange) is responsible for settlement.</li>\n<li>KYD biometric = <strong>right index finger</strong> at a CAMS PoS; the new cadre (V-B) is <strong>exempt</strong> from KYD biometrics.</li>\n<li>Employees get an <strong>EUIN</strong> under the firm's ARN, not a separate ARN; ARN minimum age is <strong>18</strong>.</li>\n<li>Due diligence triggers on <strong>any one</strong> of: &gt;20 locations, &gt;Rs 100 cr AUM, &gt;Rs 1 cr commission industry-wide, &gt;Rs 50 lakh from <strong>one AMC</strong>.</li>\n<li>Investor changes distributor: <strong>no commission to either</strong>, except when the old distributor voluntarily ceased business; investor-initiated ARN change → trail to new after a <strong>12-month</strong> cooling-off.</li>\n<li>AUM transfer to a nominee: investors get <strong>15 days</strong>, not 30, to object; the nominee needs <strong>valid ARN + KYD</strong> for an AUM transfer but <strong>no ARN</strong> just to receive commission.</li>\n<li>Additional commission is <strong>on top of</strong> trail, paid from the <strong>2 bps</strong> investor-education money, with <strong>no dual incentive</strong> for the same investor.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-b (False; institutions too), 2-b (NISM), 3-a (True).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch7", "n": 7, "title": "NAV, TER and Pricing of Units", "marks": 8, "html": "<h3>Valuation</h3>\n<h4>Valuation framework</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Valuation norms</td>\n<td><strong>Seventh Schedule</strong> (MF Regulations 2026)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Goal</td>\n<td><strong>Fair treatment</strong> of entering, exiting and staying investors</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Principles</td>\n<td><strong>10 fair valuation principles</strong>; if they <strong>conflict with the Valuation Guidelines</strong>, the <strong>Principles prevail</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Principle 1</td>\n<td>Value = <strong>realisable value</strong>, in <strong>good faith</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Policy approval</td>\n<td><strong>AMC Board</strong>; a <strong>new security type</strong> needs its valuation method set <strong>first</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Policy review</td>\n<td>By an <strong>independent auditor at least once a year</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Policy disclosure</td>\n<td>In the <strong>SAI</strong> and on the website</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Responsibility</td>\n<td>The <strong>AMC</strong>, for <strong>true and fair</strong> valuation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deviation</td>\n<td>AMC may <strong>deviate</strong> from policy (report to both <strong>Boards</strong>, disclose to investors)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Audit trail</td>\n<td>Valuation rationale kept for <strong>audit trail</strong> (<strong>Seventh Schedule</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Valuation by security type</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Security</th>\n<th>How valued</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt</td>\n<td>Trade prices from <strong>all public platforms</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Traded equity</td>\n<td><strong>Last closing price</strong> on the <strong>principal exchange</strong> (reasons in <strong>writing</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity not traded that day</td>\n<td>Use <strong>another exchange</strong>, or the <strong>earliest previous day within 30 days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>No trade for 30 days = non-traded</strong></td>\n<td>Valued <strong>in good faith</strong> by AMC Board methods; reviewed by trustees; auditors report them <strong>\"fair and reasonable\"</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Non-traded equity</td>\n<td><strong>Capitalisation of earnings</strong> (P/E of comparables) ± book value, <strong>less an illiquidity discount</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Convertibles</td>\n<td>Value the debt and equity parts <strong>separately</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Warrants</td>\n<td><strong>Share value − exercise price − discount</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gold ETF</strong></td>\n<td><strong>LBMA AM fixing</strong>, USD per troy ounce, <strong>995.0</strong> fineness</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Silver ETF</strong></td>\n<td>LBMA AM fixing, <strong>999.0</strong> fineness</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>NAV</h3>\n<h4>NAV formula</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Measure</th>\n<th>Formula</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>NAV</td>\n<td><strong>Net assets ÷ units outstanding</strong> = <strong>(total assets − liabilities other than to unitholders) ÷ units</strong></td>\n<td>Workbook: <strong>Rs 217 cr ÷ 20 cr = Rs 10.85</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>NAV rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Net assets</td>\n<td>Include <strong>unrealised gains</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Accrual principle</strong></td>\n<td>Income and expenses count when <strong>due</strong>, not when paid</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Short-term borrowing for liquidity</td>\n<td><strong>≤ 6 months</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NAV rises with</td>\n<td>More <strong>income and gains</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NAV falls with</td>\n<td>More <strong>expenses</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Mark to market</strong> stops dilution:</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Mark to market and dilution</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Action</th>\n<th>Effect</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Issuing units</td>\n<td><strong>below NAV lowers</strong> NAV for existing investors</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Redeeming</td>\n<td><strong>below NAV raises</strong> it</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Expenses and TER</h3>\n<h4>Expense rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Scheme expenses</td>\n<td>All <strong>identified and paid from the scheme</strong>, within the <strong>base expense limits</strong>, brokerage limits, transaction cost and statutory levy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Recurring expenses (<strong>allowed</strong>, (a)–(o))</td>\n<td>Marketing and <strong>distribution</strong> fees/commission, brokerage, RTA, <strong>trustee fees</strong>, audit, custodian, investor communication, <strong>fund transfer</strong>, account statements and <strong>IDCW/redemption</strong> cheques, <strong>insurance</strong>, <strong>winding up</strong>, <strong>statutory ads</strong>, <strong>storage of goods</strong> from commodity derivatives / <strong>gold and silver</strong>, <strong>listing fee</strong>, and others SEBI approves</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Spending <strong>above the base limits</strong></td>\n<td>Borne by the <strong>AMC, trustees or sponsors</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Distribution commission</td>\n<td>The <strong>AMC pays</strong>, in the manner SEBI specifies</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equity-oriented</strong> for TER</td>\n<td><strong>≥65%</strong> in equity (excluding index funds and ETFs)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>TER limits by scheme type</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scheme</th>\n<th>TER limit</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Index fund / ETF</strong></td>\n<td><strong>≤0.90%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>FoF</strong> into liquid/index/ETF</td>\n<td><strong>0.90%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>FoF <strong>≥65%</strong> into equity schemes</td>\n<td><strong>2.10%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other FoFs</td>\n<td><strong>1.85%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>FoF's own layer</td>\n<td><strong>≤2×</strong> the underlying's weighted TER</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Close-ended / interval</strong></td>\n<td>Equity <strong>1.00%</strong>, others <strong>0.80%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Open-ended TER slabs</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Slab</th>\n<th>TER % (equity / other)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>First <strong>Rs 500 cr</strong></td>\n<td><strong>2.10 / 1.85</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Next <strong>250</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1.90 / 1.65</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Next <strong>1,250</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1.60 / 1.40</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Next <strong>3,000</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1.50 / 1.25</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Next <strong>5,000</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1.40 / 1.15</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Next <strong>40,000</strong></td>\n<td><strong>−0.05% per Rs 5,000 cr</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Balance</td>\n<td><strong>0.95 / 0.70</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Charges on top of TER</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Brokerage (cash)</td>\n<td><strong>≤0.06%</strong> of trade value, on top of the limits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Brokerage (derivatives)</td>\n<td><strong>≤0.02%</strong> of trade value, on top of the limits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Total charged to investors</td>\n<td><strong>Base limit + brokerage + transaction cost + statutory levies</strong>; nothing else except <strong>exit load</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Old extra <strong>0.05%</strong> for schemes with exit load</td>\n<td><strong>Gone</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TER disclosure</td>\n<td><strong>Daily</strong> on the AMC and AMFI sites</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>AT1 and AT2 bonds</h3>\n<h4>AT1 and AT2 bond rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonds covered</td>\n<td>Bank <strong>perpetual AT1/AT2 bonds</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MF limit</td>\n<td><strong>≤10%</strong> of one issuer's bonds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scheme limit</td>\n<td><strong>≤10%</strong> of assets; <strong>≤5%</strong> in one issuer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deemed maturity of <strong>AT1</strong></td>\n<td>From <strong>1 Apr 2023 = 100 years from issue</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deemed maturity of AT2</td>\n<td><strong>AT2 = contractual maturity</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AT1 valuation</td>\n<td>On <strong>yield to call</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Close-ended debt</strong> schemes</td>\n<td><strong>Can't</strong> buy perpetuals</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Dividends (IDCW) and loads</h3>\n<h4>IDCW rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Paid from</td>\n<td><strong>Only from distributable surplus</strong>: <strong>valuation gains ignored</strong>, <strong>valuation losses deducted</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Who decides</td>\n<td><strong>Trustees</strong> decide the amount and <strong>record date</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Monthly or more frequent payouts</td>\n<td>Can be <strong>delegated to AMC officials</strong> (ratified at the <strong>next board meeting</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Public notice</td>\n<td><strong>Within 1 day</strong> of the decision; says <strong>NAV will fall</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Record date</td>\n<td><strong>5 calendar days</strong> from notice</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>No notice</strong> needed</td>\n<td><strong>Daily-to-monthly</strong> payouts in liquid and debt schemes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Late payment</strong></td>\n<td>Interest <strong>from the record date</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Payout may include <strong>capital</strong></td>\n<td>From the <strong>equalisation reserve</strong>; the split must be disclosed</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Sale and repurchase price</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Measure</th>\n<th>Formula</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Sale price</td>\n<td><strong>Entry load banned</strong>, so = <strong>NAV</strong> (+ stamp duty)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Repurchase price</td>\n<td><strong>NAV × (1 − load)</strong></td>\n<td>Rs 11 with 1% exit load = <strong>Rs 10.89</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Rs 25,000 at NAV Rs 43.21 = <strong>578.570 units</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Exit load rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>By amount</td>\n<td><strong>No distinction by amount</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Changes</td>\n<td>Apply <strong>only prospectively</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonus / IDCW-reinvestment units</td>\n<td><strong>None on bonus or IDCW-reinvestment units</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Load collected</td>\n<td>Credited <strong>back to the scheme</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Accounting and segregated portfolio</h3>\n<h4>Accounting rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Scheme accounts</td>\n<td><strong>Separate</strong> from AMC accounts, with <strong>different auditors</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NAV decimals: index, liquid and debt funds</td>\n<td><strong>4</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NAV decimals: equity and balanced funds</td>\n<td><strong>≥2</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Units</td>\n<td><strong>Fractional units</strong> allowed; exchanges may trade <strong>whole units</strong> only</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Segregated portfolio</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Segregated portfolio</strong>: management fee</td>\n<td><strong>No management fee</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other TER</td>\n<td>Only <strong>pro-rata on recovery</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NAV</td>\n<td>Declared <strong>daily</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unrated debt</td>\n<td>Can be segregated <strong>only on actual default</strong> (issuer with no rated debt)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li>If the fair valuation principles conflict with the Valuation Guidelines, the <strong>principles</strong> prevail, not the guidelines.</li>\n<li>The valuation policy is approved by the <strong>AMC Board</strong>, not the trustees, and reviewed by an independent auditor at least <strong>once a year</strong>.</li>\n<li>No trade for <strong>30 days</strong> = non-traded; non-traded equity is valued with an illiquidity <strong>discount</strong>, not a premium.</li>\n<li>Gold ETF: LBMA <strong>AM</strong> fixing at <strong>995.0</strong> fineness (USD per troy ounce); Silver ETF: LBMA AM fixing at <strong>999.0</strong>.</li>\n<li>NAV deducts liabilities <strong>other than to unitholders</strong>; net assets <strong>include</strong> unrealised gains.</li>\n<li>Issuing units below NAV <strong>lowers</strong> NAV for existing investors; redeeming below NAV <strong>raises</strong> it.</li>\n<li>Distributable surplus: valuation <strong>gains ignored</strong>, valuation <strong>losses deducted</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Trustees</strong> decide the IDCW amount and record date, not the AMC; notice within <strong>1 day</strong>, record date <strong>5 calendar days</strong> from notice.</li>\n<li>Close-ended / interval TER: equity <strong>1.00%</strong>, others <strong>0.80%</strong>; index fund / ETF <strong>0.90%</strong>.</li>\n<li>AT1 deemed maturity = <strong>100 years</strong> from issue; AT2 = <strong>contractual</strong> maturity; AT1 valued on yield to <strong>call</strong>, not maturity.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-a (SAI), 2-b (Rs 10.20), 3-a (0.90%; the workbook misprints it as \"90 percent\"), 4-c (distributable surplus).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch8", "n": 8, "title": "Taxation", "marks": 4, "html": "<ul>\n<li>Tax depends on: <strong>type of income</strong>, <strong>holding period</strong>, <strong>type of scheme</strong>, <strong>type of investor</strong>, <strong>purchase date</strong> (<strong>1 Apr 2023</strong>) and <strong>redemption date</strong> (<strong>23 Jul 2024</strong>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Basics</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>MF scheme income</td>\n<td><strong>tax exempt</strong> under <strong>Sec 10(23D)</strong>, because MFs are <strong>trusts</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Growth</strong> option</td>\n<td><strong>capital gains only</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>IDCW</strong> option</td>\n<td>Dividend <strong>+</strong> capital gains</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equity-oriented</strong> for tax</td>\n<td><strong>&gt;65%</strong> in <strong>listed Indian equity</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A <strong>FoF investing in equity MFs</strong></td>\n<td><strong>non-equity</strong> for tax</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Joint holding</td>\n<td>Income taxed in the <strong>first holder's</strong> hands</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Holding periods</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Long-term after</th>\n<th>Applies to</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>12 months</strong></td>\n<td><strong>listed securities and equity funds</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>24 months</strong></td>\n<td>Others</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Holding periods: only <strong>12 or 24 months</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Grandfathering</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Value</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Rule</td>\n<td>Gains up to <strong>31 Jan 2018</strong> exempt; cost = <strong>higher of actual cost or 31 Jan 2018 NAV</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Example</td>\n<td>Cost Rs 1 lakh, 31 Jan 2018 value Rs 2 lakh</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sold at <strong>Rs 1.8 lakh</strong></td>\n<td><strong>zero gain</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sold at <strong>Rs 2.2 lakh</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs 20,000</strong> gain</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Equity LTCG exemption</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>LTCG in the year</th>\n<th>Tax</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Exempt limit</td>\n<td>Up to <strong>Rs 1.25 lakh</strong> a year</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 90,000</td>\n<td><strong>no tax</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 1.35 lakh</td>\n<td>Tax on <strong>Rs 10,000</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Capital gains tax by scheme type</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scheme type</th>\n<th>Short-term gains</th>\n<th>Long-term gains</th>\n<th>Long-term after</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity-oriented (incl. hybrids <strong>&gt;65% equity</strong>)</td>\n<td><strong>20%</strong></td>\n<td><strong>12.5%</strong>; <strong>Rs 1.25 lakh</strong> exempt per FY</td>\n<td><strong>12 months</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt-oriented (incl. hybrids <strong>&gt;65% debt</strong>)</td>\n<td><strong>Slab rate</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Slab rate</strong></td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hybrid with <strong>35–65%</strong> domestic equity</td>\n<td><strong>Slab rate</strong></td>\n<td><strong>12.5%</strong></td>\n<td><strong>24 months</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other MFs (FoFs, international funds/FoFs)</td>\n<td><strong>Slab rate</strong></td>\n<td><strong>12.5%</strong></td>\n<td><strong>24 months</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity ETFs and Gold ETFs</td>\n<td><strong>Slab rate</strong></td>\n<td><strong>12.5%</strong></td>\n<td><strong>12 months</strong> (as printed)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt ETFs</td>\n<td><strong>Slab rate</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Slab rate</strong></td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>IDCW taxation</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>DDT</td>\n<td><strong>DDT abolished</strong> by Budget <strong>Feb 2020</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Since <strong>April 2020</strong></td>\n<td>IDCW taxed at the investor's <strong>slab rate</strong>; tax-exempt investors pay <strong>nil</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Effect on NAV</td>\n<td>IDCW <strong>reduces NAV by more</strong> than the investor's post-tax receipt</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Growth vs IDCW</td>\n<td><strong>Growth option is more tax-efficient</strong> because of <strong>tax deferral</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>From <strong>1 Apr 2021</strong></td>\n<td>IDCW is split into <strong>income distribution</strong> and <strong>capital distribution</strong> for tax</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Stamp duty</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Transaction</th>\n<th>Rate</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Issue</strong> (purchase, SIP, STP, switch-in, IDCW reinvestment)</td>\n<td><strong>0.005%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Transfer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>0.015%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Stamp duty</strong> applies from <strong>1 Jul 2020</strong>; units are allotted on the amount <strong>after stamp duty</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Capital losses</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Loss</th>\n<th>Set off against</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>STCL</strong></td>\n<td><strong>STCG or LTCG</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>LTCL</strong></td>\n<td>Only <strong>LTCG</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Any capital loss</td>\n<td><strong>Can't be set off against salary</strong> or other income heads</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unabsorbed capital loss</td>\n<td><strong>Carried forward up to 8 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Bonus stripping</strong>: loss <strong>disallowed</strong> if bought <strong>≤3 months before</strong> the record date and sold <strong>≤9 months after</strong>; the loss becomes the <strong>cost of the bonus units</strong>. Even outside this window, the practice is <strong>discouraged</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Securities Transaction Tax (STT)</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Transaction</th>\n<th>STT</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Purchase</td>\n<td><strong>None on purchase</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt funds</td>\n<td><strong>None on debt funds</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Redemption to the MF</td>\n<td><strong>0.001%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Delivery sale on exchange</td>\n<td><strong>0.001%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Non-delivery</td>\n<td><strong>0.025%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>STT</strong> applies only to <strong>equity-oriented funds</strong>, on <strong>sale or redemption</strong>; all paid by the <strong>seller</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>ELSS and Sec 80C</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>ELSS (Tax Saver)</strong></td>\n<td>80C up to <strong>Rs 1.5 lakh</strong> (individual/<strong>HUF</strong>), <strong>Old Tax Regime only</strong>, <strong>3-year lock-in</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lock-in start</td>\n<td>Runs from <strong>each SIP instalment</strong> and <strong>each IDCW reinvestment</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Who gets the tax benefit</td>\n<td>The <strong>first holder</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Under the <strong>new tax regime</strong></td>\n<td>ELSS is just an <strong>equity fund with a lock-in</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Some <strong>old retirement funds</strong></td>\n<td>Also give <strong>80C</strong>, with a <strong>5-year lock-in</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>TDS</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Investor and income</th>\n<th>TDS</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Residents</strong>, redemption</td>\n<td><strong>No TDS</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Residents, IDCW</td>\n<td><strong>10%</strong> if dividends exceed <strong>Rs 10,000</strong> a year</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NRIs</td>\n<td><strong>lower of the Income Tax Act rate or the DTAA rate</strong> (with documents)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>GST and TER</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>GST on</th>\n<th>Treatment</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Management fee</strong></td>\n<td>Charged <strong>over and above</strong> TER</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Other fees</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Within</strong> TER</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Brokerage/transaction cost</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Within</strong> TER</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Exit load</strong></td>\n<td>Deducted <strong>from the load</strong> before crediting the scheme</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Distributor commission</strong></td>\n<td>Can't be charged to the scheme</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>From <strong>1 April 2026</strong>: cost = <strong>base expense ratio + brokerage (within limits) + statutory levies (e.g. GST)</strong>. BER = advisory fees + other expenses + brokerage commission, <strong>excluding statutory levies</strong> and transaction cost; nothing else may be charged except <strong>exit load</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li>A FoF investing in equity MFs is <strong>non-equity</strong> for tax, not equity-oriented; equity-oriented = <strong>more than 65%</strong> in <strong>listed Indian</strong> equity.</li>\n<li>Hybrids with 35-65% domestic equity and other MFs (FoFs, international) turn long-term after <strong>24 months</strong>, not 12; equity funds after <strong>12 months</strong>.</li>\n<li>Grandfathering cut-off is <strong>31 Jan 2018</strong>; cost = <strong>higher</strong> of actual cost or 31 Jan 2018 NAV, not lower.</li>\n<li>Stamp duty: <strong>0.005%</strong> on issue, <strong>0.015%</strong> on transfer, from <strong>1 Jul 2020</strong>; units are allotted on the amount <strong>after</strong> stamp duty.</li>\n<li>STCL sets off against <strong>STCG or LTCG</strong>; LTCL <strong>only against LTCG</strong>; neither against salary; carry forward <strong>8 years</strong>.</li>\n<li>STT applies only on <strong>sale/redemption</strong> of <strong>equity-oriented</strong> funds and is paid by the <strong>seller</strong>; none on purchase, none on debt funds.</li>\n<li>NRI TDS is at the <strong>lower</strong> of the IT Act rate or DTAA rate, not the higher; residents have <strong>no TDS</strong> on redemption.</li>\n<li>GST on <strong>management fee</strong> is <strong>over and above</strong> TER; GST on other fees and brokerage is <strong>within</strong> TER; GST on distributor commission can't be charged to the scheme.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-b (MF income exempt), 2-a (multi-cap attracts STT).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch9", "n": 9, "title": "Investor Services", "marks": 15, "html": "<h3>NFO and plans</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Scheme idea comes from the <strong>CIO</strong> (objective) and <strong>CMO</strong> (market interest).</li>\n<li><strong>One scheme per category</strong>; exceptions: <strong>sector/thematic, index, FoF</strong>.</li>\n<li>SID approved by the <strong>trustees + AMC Board</strong>, filed with SEBI, SEBI's observations incorporated.</li>\n<li><strong>ASBA</strong>: money is only <strong>blocked</strong>, debited <strong>on allotment</strong>, keeps earning interest, <strong>no refund wait</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Trustees</strong> can reject any application <strong>without giving a reason</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>NFO timelines</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Step</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>NFO dates</td>\n<td>Open-ended: <strong>open, close, re-opening</strong>; close-ended has <strong>no re-opening date</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NFO open period</td>\n<td><strong>Min 3 working days</strong>, <strong>max 15 days</strong> (<strong>ELSS exempt</strong> from the maximum)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Allotment</td>\n<td><strong>Allot or refund within 5 business days</strong> of NFO close</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Late refund</td>\n<td><strong>15% p.a.</strong> interest, <strong>paid by the AMC</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Re-opening (open-ended)</td>\n<td><strong>Within 5 business days of allotment</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deployment</td>\n<td>Realistic deployment timelines in the SID (<strong>Reg 35(5)</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Demat credit</td>\n<td><strong>Within 2 working days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SoA</td>\n<td>Within <strong>5 business days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>NFO and ongoing pricing</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule / example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>NFO price</td>\n<td><strong>Rs 10</strong> (no entry load): units = amount ÷ 10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sale price</td>\n<td>No entry load, so <strong>sale price = NAV</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Redemption price</td>\n<td>NAV <strong>less any exit load</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ongoing purchase</td>\n<td>Rs 12,000 at Rs 12 = <strong>1,000 units</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonus 1:3</td>\n<td><strong>Bonus 1:3</strong> = 1 free unit per 3 held; NAV falls <strong>proportionately</strong>; <strong>value unchanged</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Direct and Regular plans</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Direct plan</td>\n<td><strong>Lower TER</strong>, <strong>no commission</strong>, <strong>separate NAV</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Regular plan</td>\n<td>Anything through a distributor = <strong>Regular</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Plans that can differ by expense</td>\n<td>Only <strong>two plans</strong> (Direct and Regular)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Direct application</td>\n<td>Write <strong>\"Direct\"</strong> in the <strong>ARN box</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>IDCW payout, reinvestment and growth</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Option</th>\n<th>What happens</th>\n<th>Note / example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>IDCW <strong>payout</strong></td>\n<td>Cash to bank, units <strong>unchanged</strong>, NAV falls (<strong>ex-dividend</strong> NAV)</td>\n<td><strong>Cum-dividend</strong> NAV = between announcement and payout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>IDCW <strong>reinvestment</strong></td>\n<td>Units added at <strong>ex-dividend NAV</strong></td>\n<td>Rs 2 × 100 units at NAV 20 = <strong>10 units</strong>; the Rs 200 is still <strong>taxed at slab</strong> in the year received</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Growth</strong></td>\n<td>No dividend</td>\n<td>NAV captures <strong>all gains</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Workbook illustration: NAV 10 → 12, dividend <strong>10% of face value = Re 1</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Workbook illustration: NAV 10 → 12</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Investor</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>Rs 1,200</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>B</td>\n<td>Rs 1,100 + Rs 100</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>C</td>\n<td>Reinvests at <strong>Rs 11</strong> = <strong>9.09 units</strong>; Rs 1,200</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SIF</strong>: <strong>Rs 10 lakh</strong> minimum at <strong>PAN level</strong>, across SIF strategies only.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Account statements</h3>\n<h4>Statements</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Statement</th>\n<th>When</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>SoA</td>\n<td><strong>SoA</strong> issued each month with a transaction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>No transaction in 6 months</td>\n<td>Investors with <strong>no transaction in 6 months</strong>: statement <strong>annually</strong> (or email)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CAS, transaction that month</td>\n<td><strong>CAS monthly</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CAS, no transaction</td>\n<td><strong>Half-yearly CAS</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CAS matching</td>\n<td>Investors matched by <strong>PAN</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>\"Transaction\" includes purchase, redemption, switch, IDCW payout and reinvestment, SIP, SWP, STP, <strong>bonus</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Eligible investors and the form</h3>\n<h4>Who can invest</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Investor</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Individuals</td>\n<td>Adults, up to <strong>3 joint holders</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Minors</strong></td>\n<td>Via a guardian (<strong>natural parent or court-appointed</strong>); <strong>no joint holders</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Minor's payment</td>\n<td>Only from the <strong>minor's, parent's/guardian's, or minor-guardian joint account</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>HUF</strong></td>\n<td>Via the <strong>Karta</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>NRI/PIO/OCI</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Repatriable</strong> or <strong>non-repatriable</strong> basis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>QFI</strong></td>\n<td>Must be from a <strong>FATF</strong> member and an <strong>IOSCO MMOU</strong> signatory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>FPIs</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Direct route</strong> (<strong>demat</strong>) or <strong>indirect route</strong> (<strong>UCR</strong>, Unit Confirmation Receipt)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Check <strong>\"Who can invest\"</strong> in the SID (e.g. some gilt plans only for PFs and trusts).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Holders and the application form</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>First holder</td>\n<td>The <strong>first holder</strong> gets all benefits (dividends, redemptions, tax)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>PoA holder</strong></td>\n<td>Can do everything <strong>except nominate</strong>; the grantor can still operate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Joint holders</td>\n<td><strong>Can't be added or removed</strong>, except a deletion on <strong>death</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Address</td>\n<td><strong>KYC address overrides</strong> the address on the application form</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other details</td>\n<td><strong>Occupation, income/net worth, PEP status</strong>; <strong>FATCA/CRS</strong> for foreign links</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bank details</td>\n<td>Bank details of the <strong>first holder are mandatory</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Different payout account</td>\n<td>Proof: cancelled cheque, passbook/statement <strong>≤3 months old</strong>, or bank letter</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Demat applicants</td>\n<td>Details must <strong>match the DP</strong>; <strong>DP's KYC is accepted</strong>; payout goes to the <strong>demat-linked bank account</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Nomination</td>\n<td><strong>Opt in or opt out</strong> by signed declaration; <strong>optional for joint folios</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Transactions and payments</h3>\n<h4>Transaction rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Additional purchase</td>\n<td><strong>Transaction slip</strong> (folio details <strong>override</strong> the form)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Redemption</td>\n<td>By <strong>amount or units</strong>; <strong>FIFO</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Balance below minimum</td>\n<td>The <strong>whole folio</strong> may be redeemed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Demat redemption</td>\n<td><strong>Goes through the DP</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Broker pool accounts</td>\n<td><strong>Pool accounts of brokers discontinued</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subscriptions and redemptions</td>\n<td><strong>Two-factor authentication</strong> mandatory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIF</td>\n<td>May have <strong>different subscription and redemption frequencies</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Payment modes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Mode</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>NACH</strong></td>\n<td>By <strong>NPCI</strong>; replaced <strong>ECS</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>UPI</strong></td>\n<td>Uses a <strong>VPA</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>AEPS</strong></td>\n<td>Uses <strong>Aadhaar + fingerprint</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>USSD *99#</strong></td>\n<td>Works without internet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Credit cards</td>\n<td><strong>Credit cards not allowed</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>E-wallet</strong> + <strong>cash</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs 50,000</strong> per investor <strong>per MF per FY</strong> (umbrella limit)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>E-wallet</td>\n<td>Only if loaded via <strong>cash, debit card or net banking</strong>; <strong>no third-party</strong> payments</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cash</strong></td>\n<td>Subject to conditions; only for <strong>resident individuals, sole proprietors, minors</strong> (KYC-compliant); payouts <strong>only via bank</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>OTM</strong> (One-Time Mandate)</td>\n<td>At <strong>folio level</strong>, runs on NACH, frequency <strong>\"as and when presented\"</strong>, takes <strong>3–4 weeks</strong> to register</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cheques</td>\n<td><strong>Not post-dated</strong> (except SIP), <strong>not stale</strong> (<strong>&gt;3 months</strong>), <strong>local or at-par</strong>, first holder must be an account holder</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Third-party payment exceptions</strong> (only three): minor, employer, FPI custodian.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Third-party payments</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Exception</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Minor</td>\n<td><strong>Parent or related person</strong> for a <strong>minor</strong>, up to <strong>Rs 50,000</strong> per purchase or SIP instalment</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Employer</td>\n<td><strong>Employer</strong> payroll</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>FPI</td>\n<td><strong>Custodian for FPI</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Payer conditions</td>\n<td>Third-party payer must be <strong>KYC-compliant with PAN</strong> + declaration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DD against cash</td>\n<td><strong>DD against cash ≥ Rs 50,000 rejected</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Not accepted</strong>: stock-invests, postal/money orders, outstation cheques, post-dated cheques (except SIP), cash beyond the exception.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>NRI payments and payouts</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Repatriable investment</td>\n<td>Only from <strong>NRE/FCNR</strong> (with <strong>FIRC</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Non-repatriable investment</td>\n<td>Also from <strong>NRO</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NRO-paid investment</td>\n<td><strong>NRO</strong> payouts only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NRE-paid investment</td>\n<td>Payouts to <strong>NRO or NRE</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Bank accounts and Instant Access</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Multiple bank accounts</td>\n<td><strong>5</strong> for individuals, <strong>10</strong> for non-individuals; first holder must be on each; one is <strong>default</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Payout to an <strong>unregistered</strong> account</td>\n<td>Goes to the <strong>default</strong> account</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Instant Access Facility</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Liquid and overnight</strong> schemes; <strong>lower of Rs 50,000 or 90%</strong> of value, <strong>per day per scheme per investor</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Cut-off times</h3>\n<h4>Cut-off times and applicable NAV</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Transaction</th>\n<th>Cut-off</th>\n<th>NAV applied</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equity and debt purchases (not liquid/overnight)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>3:00 pm</strong></td>\n<td>NAV of the day <strong>funds are available</strong> for use, <strong>any amount</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Liquid and overnight purchases</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1:30 pm</strong></td>\n<td>Funds in before cut-off = NAV of the <strong>day before</strong> receipt; after cut-off = NAV of the <strong>day before the next business day</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equity/debt redemption</strong></td>\n<td><strong>3 pm</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Same day</strong> NAV before; <strong>next business day</strong> after</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Liquid redemption</strong></td>\n<td><strong>3 pm</strong></td>\n<td>NAV of the <strong>day before the next business day</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Overnight redemption</strong></td>\n<td><strong>3 pm</strong>, <strong>online 7 pm</strong></td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Cut-offs <strong>don't apply</strong> to <strong>NFOs and international schemes</strong>.</li>\n<li>Liquid funds calculate NAV for <strong>every calendar day</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Time stamping</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Where</td>\n<td>At the <strong>OPoA</strong> (not when the distributor receives the form)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Machines</td>\n<td><strong>Tamper-proof</strong>; opening one is <strong>reported to trustees</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Serial numbers</td>\n<td><strong>Don't restart daily</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Non-financial requests</td>\n<td>Need only the <strong>date</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Online</td>\n<td>Time = <strong>web server time</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>KYC</h3>\n<h4>Who needs KYC and PAN exemptions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Who needs KYC</td>\n<td><strong>Everyone</strong>: joint holders, NRIs, <strong>PoA holder and issuer</strong>, <strong>guardian</strong> (not the minor)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>PAN exempt</strong></td>\n<td>Government and court officials, <strong>Sikkim</strong> residents, UN bodies, and <strong>Micro-SIP + lump sum ≤ Rs 50,000</strong> per year per MF (quote <strong>PEKRN</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Micro-SIP ID proof</td>\n<td>Includes a <strong>photo debit card</strong> (<strong>not a credit card</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Address proof</td>\n<td>In the <strong>spouse's name</strong> is accepted</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>KYC systems</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>System</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>KRA</strong></td>\n<td>One KYC across the capital market; <strong>IPV</strong> mandatory (a bank's IPV is accepted)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>CERSAI</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Central KYC Records Registry</strong> (notified <strong>26 Nov 2015</strong>); upload for individual accounts from <strong>1 Aug 2016</strong>; issues a <strong>KYC Identifier</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Aadhaar e-KYC</strong></td>\n<td>Via <strong>KUA / sub-KUA</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Online KYC</td>\n<td>Via <strong>eSign, DigiLocker, OTP, penny drop</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>KYC by investor type</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Investor</th>\n<th>Needs</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>NRI</td>\n<td><strong>PAN</strong>, passport/PIO/OCI, <strong>overseas address</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Non-individuals</td>\n<td>Eligibility, <strong>board resolution</strong>, <strong>authorised signatories</strong>, <strong>UBO</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>UBO thresholds</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Entity</th>\n<th>Threshold</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Company</td>\n<td><strong>&gt;25%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Partnership / body of individuals</td>\n<td><strong>&gt;15%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trust</td>\n<td><strong>≥15%</strong> beneficiary + settlor + trustees</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Listed company</td>\n<td><strong>Not for listed companies</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>FATCA/CRS</strong> status change reported <strong>within 30 days</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Systematic transactions</h3>\n<h4>SIP, SWP, STP, DTP and triggers</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Facility</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SIP</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rupee cost averaging</strong>: average cost <strong>below</strong> the average NAV; can start <strong>during an NFO</strong></td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SWP</strong></td>\n<td>Suits regular expenses, e.g. <strong>in retirement</strong></td>\n<td>1% load at NAV 10: <strong>101.0101 units</strong> for Rs 1,000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>STP</strong></td>\n<td>SWP from the <strong>source</strong> + SIP into the <strong>target</strong>; scheme minimums <strong>don't apply</strong>; loads and tax <strong>do</strong></td>\n<td>0.25% load on Rs 1 lakh = <strong>Rs 99,750</strong> transferred</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>DTP</strong> (dividend transfer plan)</td>\n<td>Needs the <strong>IDCW option</strong>; <strong>overrides</strong> payout/reinvest; invested the <strong>next business day after the record date</strong>; ends when source units = <strong>nil</strong></td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SIP top-up</strong></td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>+Rs 500 a year on Rs 2,500 = <strong>3,000, then 3,500</strong>; +10% = <strong>2,750, then 3,025</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Triggers</strong></td>\n<td><strong>One-time</strong>: stop-loss, appreciation, date or market-level</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>SIP rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Minor's SIP</td>\n<td>Registered <strong>only till majority</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Registration</td>\n<td>Takes <strong>15–30 days</strong>: submit 5 Sept for a 30-day lead with SIP date 15th = first debit <strong>15 Oct</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cancellation</td>\n<td>An SIP may be <strong>cancelled</strong> for <strong>insufficient funds</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Non-financial transactions</h3>\n<h4>Nomination rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Number of nominees</td>\n<td><strong>Up to 10 nominees</strong> per folio</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Frequency</td>\n<td><strong>No limit</strong> on how often a nomination can be made, changed or cancelled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Coverage</td>\n<td>The <strong>whole folio</strong>; % must total <strong>100</strong>, else <strong>equal</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Who can nominate</td>\n<td>Only <strong>individuals</strong>; <strong>not</strong> for a <strong>minor's folio</strong> or by a <strong>PoA holder</strong>; <strong>all joint holders sign</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New nomination</td>\n<td><strong>Supersedes</strong> the old one</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Demat units</td>\n<td>Follow the <strong>demat account's nomination</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Nominee's status</td>\n<td>Holds units <strong>in trust for legal heirs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Investor incapacitated</td>\n<td>Can let <strong>one adult nominee</strong> operate the folio if the investor is <strong>physically incapacitated</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Who can be a nominee</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Can be a nominee</th>\n<th>Cannot be a nominee</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Individual (even a minor or NRI)</strong></td>\n<td>Other trusts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Government or local authority</strong></td>\n<td>Society, company, firm</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Religious/charitable trust</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Karta</strong>, PoA holder</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Transmission</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Situation</th>\n<th>Units go to</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>First holder dies</td>\n<td><strong>Second holder</strong> becomes first</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Joint holder dies</td>\n<td><strong>Surviving holder(s)</strong> by <strong>name deletion</strong>, as <strong>owners</strong>, not trustees</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Single holder with nominee</td>\n<td><strong>Nominee</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Joint holder vs nominee</td>\n<td>Joint holder <strong>ranks above</strong> nominee</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>No nominee</td>\n<td><strong>Legal heirs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Documents needed</td>\n<td><strong>KYC</strong>, <strong>death certificate</strong>, <strong>indemnity</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Other changes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Change</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pledge</strong></td>\n<td>All holders sign; units must be <strong>out of lock-in</strong>; can't sell until the <strong>pledgee's NOC</strong>; the lender can redeem <strong>below the minimum</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>ISIN</strong></td>\n<td>For <strong>each option</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Demat to physical</td>\n<td><strong>Rematerialisation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Name, address, PAN, contact</td>\n<td>Via the <strong>KRA</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bank, mode of holding, nomination</td>\n<td>To <strong>each MF</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change of guardian</td>\n<td><strong>New guardian's KYC + NOC</strong> from the old guardian</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Change of Karta</strong></td>\n<td>Death certificate, bank certificate, <strong>indemnity from all co-parceners</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Minor turns major and NRI returns</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Event</th>\n<th>What happens</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Minor turns major</strong></td>\n<td>Folio <strong>frozen</strong> for the guardian; SIP/SWP/STP <strong>stop</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Minor turns major: documents</td>\n<td><strong>MAM form</strong> with PAN, KYC, bank proof, <strong>banker-attested signature</strong>, nomination, new SIP mandate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Minor turns major: IDCW</td>\n<td>IDCW payout or reinvestment <strong>continues</strong> after majority</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Minor's <strong>demat</strong></td>\n<td>Single-name, so a <strong>new demat account</strong> is needed at majority</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>NRI returns to India</strong></td>\n<td>NRE/NRO/FCNR can't be operated; open a <strong>resident account</strong> (<strong>RFC</strong> for foreign currency) and a <strong>new resident demat</strong>; update the <strong>KRA</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Turnaround times</h3>\n<h4>Turnaround times</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Deadline</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Unit certificate</td>\n<td><strong>Within 5 working days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Demat for close-ended</td>\n<td><strong>Within 2 working days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SoA or demat credit</td>\n<td>Within <strong>5 working days</strong> of NFO close or application</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Portfolio statement</strong></td>\n<td>Within <strong>10 days</strong> of the half-year</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Annual report</strong></td>\n<td>Within <strong>4 months</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Unaudited half-yearly results</strong></td>\n<td>Within <strong>1 month</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Delay interest</strong> on redemption or dividend</td>\n<td>Borne by the <strong>AMC</strong>, never the scheme</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Investor platforms and protections</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>What it is</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MITRA</strong></td>\n<td>A tracing platform for <strong>inactive and unclaimed folios</strong>, run by <strong>CAMS and KFintech</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>DigiLocker</strong></td>\n<td>Will hold MF statements; has its own <strong>nominee</strong> access</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Voluntary lock-in / debit freeze</strong></td>\n<td>SEBI, <strong>March 2026</strong>: investors can freeze demat and non-demat folios so <strong>no units can be debited</strong> until unlocked; first offered by RTAs on <strong>MF Central</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li>Late NFO refund interest at <strong>15% p.a.</strong> is paid by the <strong>AMC</strong>, not the scheme.</li>\n<li>NFO stays open <strong>min 3 working days, max 15 days</strong>; <strong>ELSS</strong> is exempt from the maximum, not the minimum.</li>\n<li>Only <strong>open-ended</strong> NFOs have a re-opening date (within <strong>5 business days of allotment</strong>); close-ended have none.</li>\n<li>IDCW reinvestment is at the <strong>ex-dividend</strong> NAV, not the cum-dividend NAV; the reinvested amount is still <strong>taxed at slab</strong>.</li>\n<li>Bonus <strong>1:3</strong> = <strong>1</strong> free unit for every <strong>3</strong> held, not 3 for 1; value is unchanged.</li>\n<li>Liquid/overnight purchase cut-off is <strong>1:30 pm</strong>; redemption cut-off is <strong>3 pm</strong> for all, with overnight online at <strong>7 pm</strong>.</li>\n<li>Instant Access Facility = the <strong>lower</strong> of Rs 50,000 or 90% of value, not the higher.</li>\n<li>UBO: company <strong>&gt;25%</strong>; partnership/body of individuals <strong>&gt;15%</strong>; trust <strong>≥15%</strong>; not for listed companies.</li>\n<li>Time stamp is at the <strong>OPoA</strong>, not when the distributor receives the form.</li>\n<li>Nominee holds units <strong>in trust for legal heirs</strong>; a surviving joint holder takes them as <strong>owner</strong>, and ranks <strong>above</strong> the nominee.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-a (ex-dividend), 2-b (bonus free), 3-c (foreign investors after KYC), 4-b (guardian), 5-d (5), 6-c (both), 7-d (any of the above), 8-a (SIF).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch10", "n": 10, "title": "Risk, Return and Performance of Funds", "marks": 7, "html": "<h3>Risk factors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>The SID lists <strong>standard (general)</strong> and <strong>specific</strong> risk factors, plus <strong>mitigation</strong>.</li>\n<li>Standard statements: past performance <strong>no guarantee</strong>; scheme <strong>name says nothing about quality</strong>; sponsor not liable beyond its <strong>initial contribution</strong>.</li>\n<li>General risks: liquidity, interest rate, <strong>reinvestment</strong> (\"interest on interest\"), political, economic, <strong>foreign currency</strong> (for FPIs; the <strong>AMC doesn't manage</strong> it), settlement/counterparty, exchange-transaction.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Risks by instrument or strategy</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Instrument / strategy</th>\n<th>Key risk</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Money market</strong> securities</td>\n<td>Liquid but <strong>no well-developed secondary market</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Securities lending</strong></td>\n<td>Borrower returns equivalent securities plus corporate benefits; risk = counterparty failure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Short-selling</strong></td>\n<td>Counterparty and <strong>illiquidity</strong> of the borrowed stock</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity by market cap</td>\n<td>Moving down from <strong>large to mid to small caps</strong> increases volatility and liquidity risk</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Derivatives</td>\n<td><strong>Leveraged</strong>; <strong>counterparty</strong> (the exchange guarantees settlement), <strong>market liquidity</strong>, <strong>model</strong> (mispricing), <strong>basis</strong> (hedge vs underlying)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt</td>\n<td>Reinvestment, <strong>rating migration</strong> (AAA → AA+ = price falls), term structure, credit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Floaters</td>\n<td><strong>Spread risk</strong> and <strong>basis risk</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Repo in corporate bonds</td>\n<td>Counterparty risk, mitigated by <strong>over-collateralisation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Segregated portfolio</td>\n<td>May be <strong>illiquid</strong>, may realise <strong>nothing</strong>, listing <strong>doesn't ensure</strong> liquidity</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Securitisation</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Point</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Structure</td>\n<td><strong>Securitisation</strong>: originator sells receivables to an <strong>SPV (trust)</strong>, which issues <strong>PTCs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pool checks</td>\n<td><strong>Lower LTV = safer</strong>; <strong>seasoning</strong> (more instalments already paid = better); <strong>DPD</strong> buckets</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Credit enhancement</strong></td>\n<td>Lets PTCs be rated <strong>above the originator</strong>; they are <strong>non-recourse</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Risks</td>\n<td><strong>Prepayment</strong>, originator bankruptcy (<strong>true sale</strong>), <strong>co-mingling</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>What MFs buy</td>\n<td>Mostly securitised paper rated <strong>AA and above</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Systematic vs unsystematic risk</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Systematic</th>\n<th>Unsystematic</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Source</td>\n<td>Market</td>\n<td>Company-specific</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Diversifiable?</td>\n<td><strong>Non-diversifiable</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Diversifiable</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Example</td>\n<td>Inflation</td>\n<td>A strike</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Investors are <strong>rewarded only for systematic risk</strong>.</li>\n<li>The fund manager can cut systematic risk only by <strong>holding cash</strong> (limited by SEBI).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Drivers of return</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Equity: <strong>security selection</strong> and <strong>market timing</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fundamental vs technical analysis</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Analysis</th>\n<th>Suits</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Fundamental analysis</strong></td>\n<td>The <strong>long term</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Technical analysis</strong> (price-volume \"<strong>chartists</strong>\")</td>\n<td>The <strong>short term and timing</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Valuation ratios</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Measure</th>\n<th>Formula / reading</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>EPS</strong></td>\n<td>PAT ÷ shares</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>P/E</strong></td>\n<td>Price ÷ EPS; <strong>forward P/E</strong> uses projected EPS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PEG</td>\n<td><strong>PEG = 1</strong> fair; <strong>&lt;1</strong> undervalued; <strong>&gt;1</strong> overvalued</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Book value/share</strong></td>\n<td>Net worth ÷ shares</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>P/BV</strong></td>\n<td>Price ÷ BV</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Dividend yield</strong></td>\n<td>DPS ÷ price; it <strong>falls in bull markets</strong>, <strong>rises in bear markets</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Growth vs value stocks</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Style</th>\n<th>Features</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Growth</strong></td>\n<td><strong>High P/E and PEG, low dividend yield</strong>; fall more in corrections</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Value</strong></td>\n<td>Priced <strong>below intrinsic value</strong>; need a <strong>long horizon</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>High <strong>valuation</strong> ≠ high <strong>price</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>EIC</strong> framework: <strong>Economy, Industry, Company</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Top-down vs bottom-up</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Approach</th>\n<th>Starts with</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Top-down</strong></td>\n<td>Economy first</td>\n<td>Avoids a bad <strong>sector</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Bottom-up</strong></td>\n<td>Stock first</td>\n<td>Sector allocation is the <strong>result</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Debt returns are driven by <strong>interest rates and credit spreads</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Debt instruments and issuers</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Instrument</th>\n<th>Issuer / tenor</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>T-bills</strong></td>\n<td>Issued by <strong>RBI</strong> for the GoI</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>CDs</strong></td>\n<td>Banks <strong>7 days–1 year</strong>, FIs <strong>1–3 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>CP</strong></td>\n<td>Companies, <strong>up to 1 year</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Bonds</strong></td>\n<td>Government issues them</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Debentures</strong></td>\n<td>Private companies issue them</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Debt return terms</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Term</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Credit spread</strong></td>\n<td>Corporate yield − <strong>gilt</strong> yield</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rating agencies</td>\n<td><strong>CRISIL, ICRA, CARE, India Ratings (Fitch)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>YTM</strong></td>\n<td>Return if <strong>held to maturity</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>HPR</strong></td>\n<td>Interest + capital gain or loss</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Floater coupon</td>\n<td><strong>Base + spread</strong>; it <strong>holds its value</strong> when rates move</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Premium example</td>\n<td>A 9.5% AAA bond when market yield is 8.5% trades at a <strong>premium</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Rate view and positioning</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rate view</th>\n<th>Action</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Rates <strong>expected up</strong></td>\n<td>Shorten duration or buy floaters</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rates <strong>expected down</strong></td>\n<td>Buy <strong>long</strong> duration</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>What drives fund returns</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Fund / asset</th>\n<th>Return driver</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt funds</td>\n<td>Hinge on <strong>interest-rate calls</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Equity funds</td>\n<td><strong>Sector and stock</strong> calls</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Liquid, ultra-short and floater funds</td>\n<td>Focus on <strong>accrual</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gold</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Global price + rupee</strong> (<strong>weaker rupee = higher</strong> return) + duties; gold funds are <strong>passive</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Real estate</strong></td>\n<td>A <strong>local</strong> asset; driven by economy, infrastructure, rates; <strong>no MF real estate schemes</strong> currently; <strong>REITs</strong> are gaining popularity with SEBI support</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Returns</h3>\n<h4>Simple and annualised return</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Measure</th>\n<th>Rule and examples</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Simple</strong> return</td>\n<td>12 → 15 = <strong>25%</strong>; 120 → 135 = <strong>12.5%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Annualised</strong></td>\n<td>Simple × 12 ÷ months: 5% in 6 months = <strong>10%</strong>; 3% in 4 months = <strong>9%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p class=\"formula\">CAGR = (Later value ÷ Initial value)<sup>1/n</sup> − 1</p>\n\n<h4>CAGR examples</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Case</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 1,000 to Rs 4,000 in 2 yrs</td>\n<td><strong>100%</strong> CAGR</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rs 10,000 at 10% for 3 yrs</td>\n<td><strong>Rs 13,310</strong> (vs <strong>13,000</strong> simple)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>n</td>\n<td><strong>Days ÷ 365</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>With dividends, SEBI uses the <strong>reinvestment method</strong> (reinvest at <strong>ex-dividend NAV</strong>): workbook example <strong>1,000 → 1,080 → 1,152 units</strong>, value <strong>Rs 17,280</strong>, <strong>43.65%</strong> over <strong>1.51 years</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Investor return ≠ scheme return</strong> because of <strong>loads</strong>, <strong>taxes</strong> and <strong>cash-flow timing</strong>; advertised returns <strong>ignore loads</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Which return to quote</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Holding period</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&lt;1 year</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Absolute</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt;1 year</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CAGR</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rolling returns</strong> = average of many consecutive periods; removes <strong>start/end-date bias</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>No promised returns</strong> except <strong>assured-return schemes</strong>, which need a named <strong>guarantor</strong> in the SID; so far <strong>no assured-return product</strong> has been launched, only <strong>capital protection-oriented</strong> funds.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Risk from the investor's view</h3>\n<h4>Investor-view risk lessons</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Point</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\"<strong>Low risk ≠ zero risk</strong>\"</td>\n<td>Liquid and ultra-short funds faced <strong>credit events</strong> in <strong>2018 and 2019</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Without segregation</td>\n<td>Redemptions <strong>raise</strong> the bad paper's share: 5% becomes <strong>10%</strong> after 50% redemptions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Arbitrage funds</td>\n<td>Those using <strong>paired arbitrage, alpha hedging, merger arbitrage</strong> take views, so they're <strong>not risk-free</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Schemes being <strong>wound up</strong></td>\n<td>Are <strong>listed</strong> (<strong>Clause 37(d)</strong> of the MF Regulations)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Real estate funds</td>\n<td><strong>High risk</strong> but <strong>less risky than direct property</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Risk measures</h3>\n<h4>Risk measures</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Measure</th>\n<th>What it shows</th>\n<th>Notes / example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Variance</strong></td>\n<td>Fluctuation vs <strong>own average</strong></td>\n<td>Workbook example <strong>0.67 vs 39.58</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SD</strong></td>\n<td><strong>√variance</strong> = <strong>total risk</strong></td>\n<td>For <strong>debt and equity</strong>; needs <strong>≥30 observations</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Beta</strong> (from <strong>CAPM</strong>)</td>\n<td><strong>Systematic</strong> risk vs a diversified index (<strong>β = 1</strong>)</td>\n<td><strong>Equity only</strong>; beta 0.8 moves <strong>8%</strong> when the market moves 10%; beta 1.2 moves <strong>12%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Modified duration</strong></td>\n<td>Interest rate sensitivity</td>\n<td>The <strong>professional's</strong> measure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>WAM</strong></td>\n<td>Simpler; used with <strong>lay investors</strong></td>\n<td>70% × 4 yrs + 30% × 1 yr = <strong>3.1 years</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Credit rating</strong> profile</td>\n<td>Default risk</td>\n<td><strong>G-secs and cash have no credit risk</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Annualising SD</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Data frequency</th>\n<th>Multiply by</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Weekly</td>\n<td><strong>×√52</strong> (0.65 → <strong>4.70%</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Monthly</td>\n<td><strong>×√12</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Daily</td>\n<td><strong>×√252</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Credit events, gating and side-pocketing</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Credit event</strong> = <strong>default, delay or downgrade</strong>.</li>\n<li>Rs 10,000 cr scheme with 8% in one paper; 20% redemptions push exposure to <strong>10%</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Gating</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rule</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>What</td>\n<td><strong>Gating</strong> = restricting redemptions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>When</td>\n<td>Only in <strong>market-wide</strong> crises (liquidity, <strong>exchange closure</strong>, operational <strong>force majeure</strong>); <strong>never for one bad security</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Limit</td>\n<td><strong>Max 10 working days in any 90 days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Approval</td>\n<td><strong>AMC Board + trustee</strong> approval; <strong>SEBI informed immediately</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>During gating</td>\n<td>The <strong>first Rs 2 lakh</strong> of every redemption is paid normally</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Segregated portfolio (side-pocketing)</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Point</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Date / status</td>\n<td><strong>Segregated portfolio</strong> (Dec <strong>2018</strong>): <strong>optional</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trigger</td>\n<td>A <strong>downgrade</strong>; unrated debt can be segregated <strong>only on actual default</strong>, after AMFI informs all AMCs (<strong>7 Nov 2019</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New schemes after <strong>7 Nov 2019</strong></td>\n<td>Must carry <strong>enabling provisions</strong> in the SID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Policy</td>\n<td>Approved by <strong>trustees</strong>; effective from the <strong>credit-event day</strong>; <strong>press release</strong> issued</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Investors</td>\n<td>Get <strong>equal units</strong> in the segregated portfolio; <strong>no subscription or redemption</strong> in it; <strong>listed within 10 working days</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New investors</td>\n<td>Get <strong>main-portfolio units only</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Costs</td>\n<td><strong>No management fee</strong>; TER only <strong>on recovery</strong>, capped at the <strong>main portfolio's average</strong>; legal costs within TER, <strong>excess borne by the AMC</strong>; <strong>never charged to the main portfolio</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Workbook example</td>\n<td>Total NAV <strong>1,000.1227</strong> = main <strong>876.2427</strong> + segregated <strong>123.88</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Mitigants: <strong>longer holding</strong> (<strong>10 yrs = almost no negative returns</strong> historically); <strong>match holding period to portfolio maturity</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li><strong>SD</strong> = total risk (debt and equity); <strong>beta</strong> = systematic risk only (equity only).</li>\n<li><strong>Systematic</strong> risk is non-diversifiable (e.g. inflation); <strong>unsystematic</strong> is diversifiable (e.g. a strike); investors are rewarded only for <strong>systematic</strong> risk.</li>\n<li>Annualise SD with <strong>√52</strong> weekly, <strong>√12</strong> monthly, <strong>√252</strong> daily, not 52, 12 or 252.</li>\n<li><strong>Technical</strong> analysis suits the short term and timing; <strong>fundamental</strong> analysis suits the long term.</li>\n<li>Dividend yield <strong>falls</strong> in bull markets and <strong>rises</strong> in bear markets.</li>\n<li>Rates expected up: <strong>shorten</strong> duration or buy floaters; rates expected down: buy <strong>long</strong> duration.</li>\n<li>Credit spread = corporate yield − <strong>gilt</strong> yield, not coupon − YTM.</li>\n<li>CP: up to <strong>1 year</strong>; CDs: banks <strong>7 days–1 year</strong>, FIs <strong>1–3 years</strong>.</li>\n<li>Gating only in <strong>market-wide</strong> crises, max <strong>10 working days in any 90 days</strong>; never for one bad security.</li>\n<li>Weaker rupee = <strong>higher</strong> gold fund return; lower LTV = <strong>safer</strong> securitised pool.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-a (True), 2-c (technical), 3-c (12.5%), 4-a (variance).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch11", "n": 11, "title": "Mutual Fund Scheme Performance", "marks": 7, "html": "<h3>Benchmarks</h3>\n<h4>Choosing a benchmark</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rule</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Must match</td>\n<td>The scheme's <strong>investment objective, asset allocation and investment strategy</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Run by</td>\n<td>An <strong>independent agency</strong>, transparently</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Past returns</td>\n<td><strong>Past returns are never</strong> a basis for choosing a benchmark</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Index fund</td>\n<td>Benchmark = <strong>the index it tracks</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Chosen by</td>\n<td>The <strong>AMC with the trustees</strong>, stated in the <strong>SID</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change</td>\n<td>Must be <strong>justified and documented</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>TRI vs PRI</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Point</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>TRI since 1 Feb 2018</strong></td>\n<td>Was PRI; TRI adds <strong>dividends/interest</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Effect</td>\n<td>Makes it look like <strong>fewer schemes beat</strong> the benchmark</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PRI–TRI gap</td>\n<td>= index dividend yield, <strong>\\~1.5–2.5%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Periods before TRI existed</td>\n<td>Use a <strong>composite CAGR</strong> (PRI then TRI)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>What decides the equity benchmark</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Factor</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Scheme type</strong></td>\n<td>Diversified vs <strong>sectoral</strong> (e.g. <strong>Bankex</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Universe</strong></td>\n<td>Large vs mid cap</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Concentration</strong></td>\n<td>Fewer stocks = <strong>Sensex 30 / Nifty 50</strong>; more = Nifty 100/200/500</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Debt indices come from <strong>CRISIL, ICICI Securities, NSE</strong>, recommended by <strong>AMFI</strong>; the list of benchmarks is on <strong>AMFI's website</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>I-Bex sub-indices</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Sub-index</th>\n<th>Range</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Si-Bex</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1–3 yrs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Mi-Bex</strong></td>\n<td><strong>3–7 yrs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Li-Bex</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&gt;7 yrs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Debt benchmarks (NSE / CRISIL)</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scheme</th>\n<th>Benchmark</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Overnight</td>\n<td><strong>NIFTY 1D Rate / CRISIL Liquid Overnight</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Liquid</td>\n<td><strong>NIFTY Liquid A-I / CRISIL Liquid Debt A-I</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Money market</td>\n<td><strong>NIFTY / CRISIL Money Market A-I</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ultra short</td>\n<td><strong>Ultra Short Duration Debt A-I</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Low duration</td>\n<td><strong>Low Duration Debt A-I</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Short duration</td>\n<td><strong>Short Duration Debt A-II</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Liquid schemes: a short-term money market benchmark such as <strong>NSE's Liquid</strong> or <strong>CRISIL Liquid Fund Index</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Equity benchmarks (NSE / BSE)</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scheme</th>\n<th>Benchmark</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi cap</td>\n<td><strong>Nifty 500 Multicap 50:25:25 / BSE 500</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Large cap</td>\n<td><strong>NIFTY 100 / BSE 100</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Large &amp; mid</td>\n<td><strong>NIFTY LargeMidcap 250 / BSE 250 LargeMidCap</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mid cap</td>\n<td><strong>Midcap 150</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Small cap</td>\n<td><strong>NIFTY Smallcap 250 / BSE 250 SmallCap</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ELSS, flexi cap, dividend yield</td>\n<td><strong>NIFTY 500 / BSE 500</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Hybrid benchmark = <strong>blend</strong>, e.g. <strong>65% Sensex + 35% I-Bex</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Hybrid benchmarks (NSE, Table 11.2)</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scheme</th>\n<th>Benchmark</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Conservative</td>\n<td><strong>NIFTY 50 Hybrid Composite Debt 15:85</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Balanced and <strong>BAF/DAA</strong></td>\n<td><strong>50:50</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Aggressive</td>\n<td><strong>65:35</strong> (or <strong>NIFTY Mid Small cap 400 TRI: 70%</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Arbitrage</td>\n<td><strong>NIFTY 50 Arbitrage</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Benchmarks for other schemes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scheme</th>\n<th>Benchmark</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gold ETF</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Price of gold</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>International funds</td>\n<td>A local index (e.g. <strong>Shanghai Composite</strong>, <strong>S&amp;P 500</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>FoF</strong> (single-fund)</td>\n<td>The <strong>underlying's</strong> benchmark</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>FoF</strong> (multi-fund)</td>\n<td>A <strong>broad market index</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Two-tier vs single benchmark</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Point</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Two-tier benchmarks</strong></td>\n<td>SEBI <strong>Oct 2021</strong>, effective <strong>1 Jan 2022</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tier 1</td>\n<td><strong>Category</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tier 2</td>\n<td><strong>Fund manager's style</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Applies to</td>\n<td><strong>Debt and equity</strong> schemes; all must be <strong>TRI</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Single benchmark</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Hybrid/solution, sectoral, index/ETF</strong> schemes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Debt Tier-1 benchmarks</td>\n<td>Follow <strong>PRC</strong>, from <strong>1 Apr 2022</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Performance measures</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Relative return</strong> vs benchmark or peers <strong>ignores risk</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>AMCs and trustees</strong> review relative returns <strong>periodically</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"formula\">Sharpe = (R<sub>s</sub> − R<sub>f</sub>) ÷ SD &nbsp;·&nbsp; Treynor = (R<sub>s</sub> − R<sub>f</sub>) ÷ Beta &nbsp;·&nbsp; IR = (R<sub>p</sub> − R<sub>b</sub>) ÷ SD of excess return</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>R<sub>s</sub> − R<sub>f</sub> = <strong>risk premium</strong>; the risk-free rate = <strong>T-bill</strong> return.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Risk-adjusted measures</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Measure</th>\n<th>Formula / basis</th>\n<th>Example / use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sharpe</strong></td>\n<td>Uses <strong>SD</strong> (total risk)</td>\n<td>(7 − 5) ÷ 0.5 = <strong>4</strong>; higher = better; compare <strong>like with like</strong> (never equity vs debt)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Treynor</strong></td>\n<td>Uses <strong>beta</strong> (systematic risk)</td>\n<td>(8 − 5) ÷ 1.2 = <strong>2.5</strong>; for <strong>diversified equity</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Alpha</strong></td>\n<td>Actual − <strong>beta-expected (optimal)</strong> return</td>\n<td><strong>Positive = outperformance</strong>; for diversified equity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Information Ratio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Excess return over the Tier-1 benchmark ÷ SD of excess return</strong> (daily data)</td>\n<td>The <strong>only mandatory</strong> risk-adjusted measure; disclosed <strong>daily</strong> on the AMC and AMFI sites (<strong>Jan 2025</strong> circular)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Tracking error</strong></td>\n<td><strong>SD of excess returns</strong></td>\n<td>Index fund: how closely it tracks its index (<strong>ideally zero</strong>); active fund: how <strong>consistently</strong> it beats its benchmark (<strong>lower = more consistent</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Risk-adjusted <strong>\"calculations are arithmetic; evaluation is an art\"</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Disclosure sources</h3>\n<h4>Where performance is disclosed</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Source</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SID</strong></td>\n<td>Updated (with performance) <strong>twice a year</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Factsheet</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Monthly</strong> but <strong>not mandatory</strong>; ad rules apply to it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Product label</td>\n<td>Shows the <strong>objective</strong> (wealth creation / income / liquidity), <strong>asset class</strong>, <strong>holding period</strong> and <strong>risk-o-meter</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>AMFI website</strong></td>\n<td>Performance data for <strong>all schemes</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Data vendors</td>\n<td>Include <strong>Morningstar and Value Research</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Discrete annual returns</strong> show <strong>consistency</strong> across market conditions.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Factsheet macro readings</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Signal</th>\n<th>Effect</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>High <strong>fiscal deficit</strong></td>\n<td>Pushes <strong>interest rates up</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Inflation</strong> above comfort</td>\n<td>Brings <strong>monetary tightening</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Low <strong>global rates</strong></td>\n<td>Pull <strong>flows into emerging markets</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Oil</strong> prices</td>\n<td>Move the <strong>currency</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li><strong>Sharpe</strong> divides by <strong>SD</strong> (total risk); <strong>Treynor</strong> divides by <strong>beta</strong> (systematic risk); both share the numerator (scheme return − T-bill return).</li>\n<li>Information Ratio = excess return over the <strong>Tier-1 benchmark</strong> ÷ SD of that excess return, not (scheme return − T-bill return).</li>\n<li><strong>Tier 1 = category</strong>, <strong>Tier 2 = fund manager's style</strong>, not the other way round.</li>\n<li>TRI since <strong>1 Feb 2018</strong>; two-tier benchmarks effective <strong>1 Jan 2022</strong> (circular Oct 2021); debt Tier-1 on PRC from <strong>1 Apr 2022</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Si-Bex 1–3 yrs</strong>, <strong>Mi-Bex 3–7 yrs</strong>, <strong>Li-Bex &gt;7 yrs</strong>.</li>\n<li>IR is the <strong>only mandatory</strong> risk-adjusted measure, disclosed <strong>daily</strong> on AMC and AMFI sites, not Sharpe and not monthly.</li>\n<li>Factsheet is <strong>monthly but not mandatory</strong>; the SID (with performance) is updated <strong>twice a year</strong>.</li>\n<li>Single-fund FoF uses the <strong>underlying's</strong> benchmark; multi-fund FoF uses a <strong>broad market index</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Lower</strong> tracking error = more consistent outperformance; an index fund's tracking error is ideally <strong>zero</strong>.</li>\n<li>Benchmark is chosen by the <strong>AMC with the trustees</strong>, never on <strong>past returns</strong>; a change must be justified and documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-d (Sharpe), 2-d (past returns), 3-a (TRI), 4-b (tracking error).</p>\n"}, {"id": "ch12", "n": 12, "title": "Mutual Fund Scheme Selection", "marks": 15, "html": "<h3>Investor fit</h3>\n<h4>Steps</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Step</th>\n<th>Action</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Step 1</td>\n<td><strong>Set goals</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Step 2</td>\n<td><strong>Assess situation and risk appetite</strong> (<strong>need + ability + willingness</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Needs map to funds</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Need</th>\n<th>Fund</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Growth</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Equity</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Income</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Debt</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Parking</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Liquid</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Equity needs a <strong>long horizon</strong>, even for an investor willing to take risk.</li>\n<li><strong>Age alone is a poor guide</strong>; use the <strong>time horizon to each goal</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Core vs satellite</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Portfolio</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n<th>Examples</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Core</strong></td>\n<td>Long-term goals</td>\n<td>Diversified, large, mid cap</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Satellite</strong></td>\n<td>Tactical</td>\n<td><strong>Sector funds</strong>, <strong>long gilt</strong> (rates expected down), <strong>gold</strong> (high inflation or uncertainty)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Workbook illustration: a moderate investor at <strong>80% core / 20% satellite</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Risk hierarchies (left to right)</h3>\n<h4>Risk orderings</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Dimension</th>\n<th>Order (left to right)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Overall: <strong>risk and return rise</strong></td>\n<td>Liquid → debt → hybrid → equity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Interest rate risk rises</strong></td>\n<td>Overnight → liquid → ultra-short → low → short → medium → medium-long → long</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Credit risk rises</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Gilt</strong> → banking &amp; PSU → corporate bond → <strong>credit risk fund</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equity risk falls</strong></td>\n<td>Small → mid → multi → large &amp; mid → <strong>large</strong> (lowest)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Concentration risk rises</strong></td>\n<td>Diversified → <strong>focused</strong> → thematic → <strong>sector</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hybrid risk rises</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arbitrage</strong> → <strong>conservative</strong> → equity savings → dynamic asset allocation → multi-asset → balanced → <strong>aggressive</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Product labelling</strong> (2013) added a disclaimer to <strong>consult a financial adviser</strong> if unsure of suitability; the <strong>risk-o-meter</strong> is covered in Ch 5.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Choosing by strategy</h3>\n<h4>Passive vs active</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Key points</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Passive</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No selection risk</strong>, lower cost, but <strong>NAV still falls</strong> when the index falls</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Active</strong></td>\n<td>Higher cost and risk; must <strong>beat the benchmark</strong> to justify the choice</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Open-ended vs close-ended</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Structure</th>\n<th>Key points</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Open-ended</td>\n<td>Liquidity at <strong>NAV less load</strong>, but must hold some <strong>cash</strong> (dilutes returns) and faces <strong>flow pressure</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Close-ended</td>\n<td>Exit only via the exchange, often at a <strong>discount with no limit</strong>; price <strong>converges to NAV near maturity</strong>; can hold <strong>illiquid or long-gestation</strong> stocks; choose only if the money can stay <strong>locked in</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Equity fund choices</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Fund</th>\n<th>When / risk</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Index or value</strong> fund</td>\n<td>Low-risk equity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Growth</strong> fund</td>\n<td>Extra risk for extra return; outperforms in <strong>bull</strong> markets</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Value</strong></td>\n<td>Outperforms in <strong>falling</strong> markets <strong>or over a long period</strong>; needs a <strong>long horizon</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Focused</td>\n<td><strong>Riskier than diversified</strong> but <strong>less risky than sector</strong> funds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sector</strong></td>\n<td>Depend on <strong>timing</strong>, so belong in the <strong>satellite</strong> portfolio</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thematic</strong> (MNC, PSU, infra)</td>\n<td>Sit <strong>between diversified and sector</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mid/small caps</td>\n<td>Shine in <strong>recoveries</strong>, when large caps turn expensive, but many <strong>fail in downturns</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>International funds</strong></td>\n<td>Foreign equity + <strong>currency</strong>: a <strong>stronger dollar helps</strong> an Indian investor; suit the <strong>satellite</strong> portfolio</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>\"<strong>Diversification is protection against ignorance.</strong>\"</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Debt fund choices</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Fund</th>\n<th>When / risk</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>FMP</strong></td>\n<td>Horizon must <strong>match maturity</strong>; more <strong>predictable</strong> returns than FDs; check <strong>credit risk</strong>; exit before maturity <strong>only via exchange</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>TMFs</strong></td>\n<td>Replacing FMPs: G-secs, SDLs, <strong>AAA PSU</strong> paper; <strong>liquid</strong> via the AMC</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Short duration (1–3 yrs)</strong></td>\n<td>Use when rates are <strong>expected to rise</strong>; low volatility; core for low-risk investors</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Liquid fund</strong></td>\n<td>Lowest risk; compares to a <strong>savings account</strong>; for parking <strong>up to 91 days</strong>; using it longer <strong>wastes return</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Floater</strong></td>\n<td>NAV stays <strong>steady</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Duration-managed</strong> debt funds</td>\n<td><strong>More volatile</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Hybrid and gold choices</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Fund</th>\n<th>Point</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Hybrid funds</td>\n<td>Judge the <strong>equity quality</strong> and the <strong>debt credit/duration</strong> separately; \"<strong>conservative\" refers only to equity allocation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dynamic asset allocation</td>\n<td>Be <strong>cautious with dynamic asset allocation</strong> funds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Balanced fund</td>\n<td>Tax status depends on its <strong>equity share</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gold ETF</strong></td>\n<td>Tracks the <strong>gold price</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gold sector fund</strong></td>\n<td>Holds <strong>mining shares</strong>, which rise and fall <strong>more</strong> and move with company factors</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Choosing within a category</h3>\n<h4>Selection checks</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Check</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>True to label</td>\n<td>Portfolio must be <strong>true to label</strong> (e.g. a \"value\" fund full of expensive front-line stocks isn't)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Performance</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Consistent</strong> outperformance, <strong>downside protection</strong>, vs <strong>benchmark and peers</strong>, over <strong>rolling</strong> periods</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Fund age</strong></td>\n<td>Matters most where scheme returns <strong>diverge</strong> (e.g. <strong>multi cap</strong> more than large cap)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Fund size</strong></td>\n<td>Large helps <strong>large-cap</strong> funds; hurts <strong>mid-cap or sector</strong> funds with limited stocks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Costs</strong></td>\n<td>Matter most in <strong>debt</strong> and <strong>index</strong> funds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Star ratings</td>\n<td>= <strong>Past performance</strong>, <strong>no predictive</strong> power; this quarter's best fund is rarely next quarter's</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Target</td>\n<td>The <strong>top few</strong> consistently: <strong>top 3–5</strong> in small categories, <strong>top 10–15%</strong> in big ones</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Look-back periods</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Fund</th>\n<th>Look-back</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equity</strong></td>\n<td><strong>≥ 5 yrs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Long-term debt</strong></td>\n<td><strong>≥ 3 yrs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Short-term debt</strong></td>\n<td>Shorter</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Liquid funds</strong></td>\n<td><strong>7 days, 15 days, 1 month</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Portfolio turnover</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Formula</td>\n<td>Purchases <strong>or</strong> sales (<strong>whichever is lower</strong>) ÷ average net assets</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Example</td>\n<td><strong>10,000 ÷ 5,000 = 200%</strong>, average holding <strong>6 months</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Judge against <strong>style</strong></td>\n<td>6 months is too short for <strong>value</strong>, fine for <strong>momentum</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Options and do's and don'ts</h3>\n<h4>IDCW vs SWP vs growth</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Option</th>\n<th>Point</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>IDCW payout</strong></td>\n<td>Gives cash flow but <strong>not assured</strong> (needs distributable surplus); taxed at <strong>slab</strong>; IDCW suits only <strong>tax-exempt</strong> investors</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SWP</td>\n<td>For regular income, <strong>SWP is better</strong> than IDCW (capital gains tax, plus <strong>STT</strong> on equity)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Growth</strong></td>\n<td>Compounds <strong>pre-tax</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Book gains or losses to <strong>set off</strong> against others.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Do's and don'ts</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Do / Don't</th>\n<th>Rule</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Do</td>\n<td>Ensure <strong>suitability</strong> (<strong>PFUTP</strong>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Do</td>\n<td>Stick to <strong>asset allocation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Do</td>\n<td>Understand <strong>objective and strategy</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Do</td>\n<td>Watch <strong>taxes and loads</strong> on redemption</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Do</td>\n<td>Keep a <strong>written, consistent</strong> selection method</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Don't</td>\n<td><strong>Chase past performance</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h4>Conduct and disclosure rules</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rule</th>\n<th>Detail</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Code of conduct for AMCs and trustees</td>\n<td><strong>Fourth Schedule</strong> (Appendix 1): <strong>equitable treatment</strong> of all unitholder classes (favouring one set is not fair), no excessive concentration with brokers or <strong>few investors</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Regulated entities and their agents (incl. <strong>MFDs</strong>)</td>\n<td>Show their <strong>registered name and registration number</strong> on their <strong>social media home page</strong> and at the <strong>start of every video/content</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3>Exam traps</h3>\n<ul class=\"traps\">\n<li>Equity risk is <strong>lowest in large cap</strong>, then large &amp; mid, multi, mid, and <strong>highest in small cap</strong>; large &amp; mid is less risky than multi cap, not more.</li>\n<li>Credit risk rises <strong>gilt → banking &amp; PSU → corporate bond → credit risk fund</strong>; banking &amp; PSU is below corporate bond, not above.</li>\n<li>Concentration risk: diversified &lt; focused &lt; <strong>thematic</strong> &lt; <strong>sector</strong>; thematic sits between diversified and sector, not above sector.</li>\n<li>Hybrid risk starts at <strong>arbitrage</strong> (lowest), not conservative, and ends at <strong>aggressive</strong>, which is above balanced.</li>\n<li>Long gilt is a satellite bet when rates are expected to <strong>fall</strong>; short duration (1-3 yrs) is used when rates are expected to <strong>rise</strong>.</li>\n<li>Liquid funds are for parking <strong>up to 91 days</strong>, not longer; holding them longer wastes return.</li>\n<li><strong>Growth</strong> outperforms in <strong>bull</strong> markets; <strong>value</strong> outperforms in <strong>falling</strong> markets or over a long period, not in bull runs.</li>\n<li>A <strong>stronger</strong> dollar helps an Indian investor in an international fund, not a weaker one; international funds are <strong>satellite</strong>, not core.</li>\n<li>Turnover numerator = <strong>lower</strong> of purchases or sales, not the higher; 200% turnover = about <strong>6 months</strong> holding (too short for value, fine for momentum).</li>\n<li>Look-back: equity <strong>at least 5 yrs</strong>, long-term debt <strong>at least 3 yrs</strong>; target top <strong>3-5</strong> in small categories, top <strong>10-15%</strong> in big ones, not the reverse.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workbook sample answers:</strong> 1-d (gilt), 2-a (risk-o-meter), 3-b (False), 4-a (multi-cap), 5-a (FMPs), 6-a (True), 7-c (both).</p>\n"}];
